(()=>{const pages={"calc":"\u003csection class=\"page\" data-page=\"calc\" id=\"calc\">\n \u003cdiv class=\"home\" id=\"home\">\u003cdiv class=\"wrap hA\">\u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Diesel or electric: what will your commercial vehicle cost?\u003c/h1>\u003cdiv class=\"hAg\">\u003cdiv class=\"hAl\">\u003cdiv class=\"hch\" role=\"radiogroup\" aria-label=\"Your situation\">\u003cbutton type=\"button\" role=\"radio\" data-hc=\"h\" aria-checked=\"false\">\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M7 4v16M17 4v16M3 8l4-4 4 4M13 16l4 4 4-4\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003cb>Replace your current diesel\u003c/b>\u003cspan>Keep it or replace it now?\u003c/span>\u003c/button>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" role=\"radio\" data-hc=\"n\" aria-checked=\"false\">\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003cb>Buy or lease a new commercial vehicle\u003c/b>\u003cspan>Diesel or electric?\u003c/span>\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"vts\" role=\"radiogroup\" aria-label=\"Vehicle\">\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"vt\" role=\"radio\" data-vt=\"trekker\" aria-checked=\"true\">\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M2 4h35v13H2z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M33 19.5h10\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M42 21V7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h7l5 7.5h2.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 1.5 1.5V21z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M45 12.5h7\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"9\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"16\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"38\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"53\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003cb>Tractor unit\u003c/b>\u003csmall>N3 · with semi-trailer\u003c/small>\u003c/button>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"vt\" role=\"radio\" data-vt=\"bakwagen\" aria-checked=\"false\">\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003cb>Rigid truck\u003c/b>\u003csmall>N2 or N3 · distribution\u003c/small>\u003c/button>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"vt\" role=\"radio\" data-vt=\"bestel\" aria-checked=\"false\">\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M8 21V9a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h26l10 8h6a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v4z\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"18\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"47\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003cb>Van\u003c/b>\u003csmall>N1 · up to 3,500 kg\u003c/small>\u003c/button>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"vt\" role=\"radio\" data-vt=\"bus\" aria-checked=\"false\">\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M3 5h54a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v13H3z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M3 12h57\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"49\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003cb>Bus\u003c/b>\u003csmall>M3 · regional bus or coach\u003c/small>\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003caside class=\"hx\" data-mx=\"156433\" aria-label=\"Example calculation for a tractor unit\">\u003cp class=\"hxh\">Electric \u003cb data-tw=\"hx\">€ 41.306\u003c/b> cheaper\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"hks\">\u003clabel for=\"hkm\">At \u003cb id=\"hkV\">100.000\u003c/b> km per year\u003c/label>\u003cinput id=\"hkm\" class=\"hkr\" type=\"range\" min=\"40000\" max=\"150000\" step=\"5000\" value=\"100000\">\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"hkw\">\u003cp class=\"hkh\">Total cost per year\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"hkb\">\u003cspan>Diesel\u003c/span>\u003ci>\u003cu data-bar=\"d\" style=\"width:72.04879607926699%\">\u003c/u>\u003c/i>\u003cb id=\"hkD\">€ 112.708\u003c/b>\u003cspan>Electric\u003c/span>\u003ci class=\"e\">\u003cu data-bar=\"e\" style=\"width:45.644044321329645%\">\u003c/u>\u003c/i>\u003cb id=\"hkE\">€ 71.403\u003c/b>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003cp class=\"hxv\" id=\"hkT\">Difference: \u003cb>€ 41.306\u003c/b>\u003c/p>\u003c/aside>\u003c/div>\u003cbutton class=\"cta big hgo\" type=\"button\" data-start>Start calculating \u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\u003cnoscript>\u003cp class=\"wrap\">The calculator needs JavaScript. You can browse the models and switching guide without JavaScript.\u003c/p>\u003c/noscript>\u003c/div>\n \u003cdiv class=\"hgw\">\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap home uv\" id=\"uv\" data-no-translate>\n  \u003csection class=\"uvS uvI\" data-s=\"idee\">\u003cheader>\u003ch2>What Stekker of Diesel does\u003c/h2>\u003c/header>\u003cdiv>\u003cp>What does an electric van or truck cost compared with diesel? Compare costs per km and per year using your own mileage, energy prices and ownership period. Include charging infrastructure and finance where relevant to your investment.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Free, no account and no sales pitch.\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\u003c/section>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"uvtab\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Help\">\u003cbutton type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-uvt=\"kost\" aria-selected=\"true\">All costs\u003c/button>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-uvt=\"omslag\" aria-selected=\"false\">Cheaper from\u003c/button>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-uvt=\"tijd\" aria-selected=\"false\">What is changing\u003c/button>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-uvt=\"onaf\" aria-selected=\"false\">Independent\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\n  \u003csection class=\"uvS uvP\" data-s=\"kost\">\u003cheader>\u003ch2>All costs, not just fuel\u003c/h2>\u003cp id=\"uvKh\">\u003c/p>\u003c/header>\u003cdiv id=\"uvK\">\u003c/div>\u003c/section>\n  \u003csection class=\"uvS uvP\" data-s=\"omslag\">\u003cheader>\u003ch2>Where diesel still wins\u003c/h2>\u003cp id=\"uvOh\">\u003c/p>\u003c/header>\u003cdiv class=\"uvo\" id=\"uvO\">\u003c/div>\u003c/section>\n  \u003csection class=\"uvS uvP\" data-s=\"tijd\">\u003cheader>\u003ch2>What is changing\u003c/h2>\u003cp id=\"uvTh\">\u003c/p>\u003c/header>\u003cdiv id=\"uvT\">\u003c/div>\u003c/section>\n  \u003csection class=\"uvS uvP\" data-s=\"onaf\">\u003cheader>\u003ch2>Independent\u003c/h2>\u003cp>No dealer, no leasing company, no account.\u003c/p>\u003c/header>\u003cdiv>\u003cdl class=\"uvl\" id=\"uvL\">\u003c/dl>\u003cp class=\"uvn\">Prices as of October 2026. You can change everything in the calculator. \u003ca href=\"/en/about/\">How we calculate\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\u003c/section>\n  \u003csection class=\"uvS\" data-s=\"faq\">\u003cheader>\u003ch2>FAQs\u003c/h2>\u003c/header>\u003cdiv class=\"faq\">\n   \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Is an electric truck cheaper than a diesel?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Over the full ownership period it often is, especially at high mileage. An electric tractor unit or rigid truck costs more to buy but less in energy, maintenance and the Dutch truck charge. Whether that adds up for you depends on your mileage, your electricity price and the grant.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n   \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Is an electric van cheaper than diesel?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>At average use they are close, and at low mileage diesel often still wins. Vans pay no truck charge, so the difference mostly comes from energy and maintenance. If you drive into cities, also check the \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/zero-emission-zones/\">zero-emission zones\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n   \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>What are the total costs of a vehicle?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>All costs during ownership, often called TCO (total cost of ownership). Dus de Purchase min Grant and residual value, plus Energy, Maintenance, Insurance, Road tax and heffing. Alleen de brandstofprijs Compare geeft One vertekend beeld.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n   \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Which grants are there for an electric truck?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Tractor units and rigid trucks can get AanZET, or otherwise the MIA. SPRILA may apply to a charger. Amounts and conditions are under \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/grants/\">Grants and tax schemes\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n   \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Does electric suit my routes?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>That depends on your longest daily route, where you can charge and how much power your grid connection has. Check it under \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/range-planning/\">Range\u003c/a> and \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/grid-capacity/\">Grid congestion\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n  \u003c/div>\u003c/section>\n\u003csection class=\"uvS\">\u003cheader>\u003ch2>Multiple vehicles\u003c/h2>\u003c/header>\u003cdiv>\u003ch3>\u003ca href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\">Electrify your fleet\u003c/a>\u003c/h3>\u003cp>Assess costs, charging capacity and replacement dates together for each vehicle. Request an introductory consultation for a plan based on your own routes.\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\u003c/section>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"uvend\">\u003cbutton class=\"cta\" type=\"button\" data-start>Start calculating \u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\n \u003c/div>\n \u003cbutton class=\"cta big hgo hgm\" type=\"button\" data-start>Start calculating \u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/button>\n \u003c/div>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap\">\n  \u003cdiv class=\"intro\">\n   \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Diesel or electric? Calculate your cost per km\u003c/h1>\n   \u003cnav class=\"mode\" aria-label=\"Calculation mode\">\u003ca href=\"/en/\" data-mode=\"b\" aria-current=\"page\">Simple\u003c/a>\u003ca href=\"/en/detailed-calculation/\" data-mode=\"x\">Detailed\u003c/a>\u003c/nav>\n  \u003c/div>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"pick\" aria-label=\"Vehicle\" data-vts>\u003c/div>\n \u003c/div>\n\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap cg\" id=\"cg\">\n  \u003cdiv class=\"cmain\">\n   \u003cdiv id=\"res\">\u003c/div>\n   \u003cdiv class=\"board\" id=\"board\" aria-live=\"polite\">\u003c/div>\n   \u003cdiv class=\"scn\" id=\"scn\" hidden>\u003c/div>\n   \u003csection class=\"story\" id=\"story\" aria-label=\"Assumptions\">\n    \u003cinput type=\"hidden\" id=\"plk\" value=\"\">\n    \u003cdiv class=\"sum\" id=\"sum\">\u003c/div>\n    \u003cbutton class=\"lnk\" type=\"button\" data-reset id=\"sumRs\" hidden>Reset example figures\u003c/button>\n   \u003c/section>\n   \u003cdiv class=\"ins\" id=\"ins\">\u003c/div>\n\n\n\n  \u003c/div>\n \u003c/div>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap emb\">\u003ca href=\"https://stekkerofdiesel.nl/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Stekker of Diesel\u003cspan aria-hidden=\"true\">↗\u003c/span>\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\n \u003ca class=\"fcta\" id=\"fcta\" href=\"/en/detailed-calculation/\" data-xgo hidden>Calculate with your own figures \u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/a>\n\n\u003c/section>","uitgebreid":"\u003csection class=\"page\" data-page=\"uitgebreid\" hidden>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap\">\n  \u003cdiv class=\"intro\">\n   \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Total costs and payback: diesel or electric\u003c/h1>\n   \u003cnav class=\"mode\" aria-label=\"Calculation mode\">\u003ca href=\"/en/\" data-mode=\"b\">Quick results\u003c/a>\u003ca href=\"/en/detailed-calculation/\" data-mode=\"x\" aria-current=\"page\">Detailed results\u003c/a>\u003c/nav>\n  \u003c/div>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"xsum\" id=\"xSum\">\u003c/div>\n \u003c/div>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap\">\u003cdiv id=\"resX\">\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap\">\n  \u003cdiv class=\"cmain\">\n   \u003csection class=\"vs\" aria-labelledby=\"hVs\">\n    \u003cdiv class=\"vsh\">\u003ch2 id=\"hVs\">Cost breakdown\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"seg sm\" id=\"unit\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Unit\">\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"vsl\">\n     \u003cdiv class=\"grid3 colh\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cspan class=\"cd\">Diesel\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"cm\">\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"ce\">Electric\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\n     \u003cdiv id=\"rows\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003cdiv id=\"xrows\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"grid3 tot\">\u003cspan class=\"rd\">\u003cb class=\"rv\" id=\"vD-tot\">\u003c/b>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"rl\">\u003cb>Total\u003c/b>\u003csmall id=\"df-tot\">\u003c/small>\u003c/span>\u003cspan class=\"re\">\u003cb class=\"rv\" id=\"vE-tot\">\u003c/b>\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\n    \u003c/div>\n   \u003c/section>\n\n   \u003cdiv id=\"xEx1\">\u003c/div>\n\n   \u003csection class=\"an\" id=\"xAn\" aria-labelledby=\"hAn\">\n    \u003ch2 id=\"hAn\">Payback period\u003c/h2>\n    \u003cdiv id=\"pbX\">\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"pbsw\" id=\"pbS\">\u003c/div>\n   \u003c/section>\n\n   \u003cdiv id=\"xEx2\">\u003c/div>\n\n   \u003csection class=\"an\" aria-labelledby=\"hSn\">\n    \u003ch2 id=\"hSn\">If prices change\u003c/h2>\n    \u003cp class=\"snp\">The annual mileage and energy prices at which electric becomes cheaper.\u003c/p>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"snw\" id=\"snX\">\u003c/div>\n   \u003c/section>\n\n   \u003csection class=\"add\" aria-labelledby=\"hAdd\">\u003cdiv class=\"addt\">\u003ch2 id=\"hAdd\">Additional costs\u003c/h2>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"addl\" id=\"addL\">\u003c/div>\u003c/section>\n\n   \u003ca class=\"fln\" id=\"xFln\" href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\" data-fleet=\"calc\">\u003cspan class=\"flv\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003csvg class=\"g\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M8 21V9a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h26l10 8h6a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v4z\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"18\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"47\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003csvg class=\"g\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003csvg class=\"g\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M2 4h35v13H2z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M33 19.5h10\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M42 21V7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h7l5 7.5h2.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 1.5 1.5V21z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M45 12.5h7\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"9\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"16\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"38\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"53\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003csvg class=\"a\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003csvg class=\"a\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M8 21V9a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h26l10 8h6a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v4z\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"18\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"47\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003csvg class=\"a\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M2 4h35v13H2z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M33 19.5h10\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M42 21V7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h7l5 7.5h2.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 1.5 1.5V21z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M45 12.5h7\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"9\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"16\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"38\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"53\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/span>\u003cdiv>\u003cspan>Fleet analysis\u003c/span>\u003cb>Calculating for more than one vehicle?\u003c/b>\u003cem>We calculate your whole fleet and turn it into a plan.\u003c/em>\u003c/div>\u003ci>Book an intro call\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/i>\u003c/a>\n\n   \u003caside class=\"ad band\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\">Advertisement\u003c/aside>\n\n   \u003ca class=\"rhgo xback\" href=\"/en/\">\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M20 12H5M11 6l-6 6 6 6\"/>\u003c/svg>Quick results\u003c/a>\n\n   \u003cdiv class=\"more\">\n    \u003cdetails id=\"wfD\" hidden>\u003csummary>\u003cb>How do additional costs affect savings?\u003c/b>\u003c/summary>\u003cdiv id=\"wfX\" style=\"padding-top:24px\">\u003c/div>\u003c/details>\n    \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>\u003cb>Good to know\u003c/b>\u003c/summary>\u003cdl class=\"facts\" id=\"facts\">\u003c/dl>\u003c/details>\n    \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>\u003cb>About the figures\u003c/b>\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Example purchase prices, consumption, battery capacity, maintenance, insurance and residual values vary by make, configuration and use. Replace them with your own quotes and operating figures.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Truck toll applies only to N2 and N3 trucks over 3,500 kg. The calculator uses the statutory 2027 rates: €0.206/km diesel and €0.040/km electric for a tractor unit over 32 tonnes; €0.187 and €0.037 for an 18–32-tonne rigid truck. AanZET is a capped percentage of purchase price depending on category and company size. MIA estimates a 36% extra deduction on 90% of purchase price, at 19% or 25.8% corporation tax. AanZET and MIA cannot be combined.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Range is usable battery capacity divided by consumption. Cold weather and heavy loads reduce it. Daily distance is annual mileage divided by operating days.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Well-to-wheel CO₂ factors from CO2emissiefactoren.nl: 3.27 kg per litre of diesel and 0.48 kg per kWh of grid electricity. Driver costs, overheads and VAT are excluded.\u003c/p>\u003cp>All figures under Additional costs are adjustable assumptions: interest, return on equity, grid connection, charger maintenance and standing charges, foreign tolls, and the price and time cost of public charging. Check toll rates with each national operator.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n   \u003c/div>\n \u003c/div>\n \u003c/div>\n\u003c/section>","modellen":"\u003csection class=\"page\" data-page=\"modellen\" hidden>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap\">\n  \u003cdiv class=\"phead\">\u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Electric vehicles\u003c/h1>\u003cp class=\"seo-intro\" id=\"mIntro\">\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"mtools\">\n   \u003cdiv class=\"seg sm mcat\" id=\"mCat\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Vehicle\">\u003c/div>\n   \u003clabel class=\"msearch\" for=\"mSearch\">\u003cinput id=\"mSearch\" type=\"search\" placeholder=\"Search make or vehicle\" aria-label=\"Search make or vehicle\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-controls=\"mList\">\u003c/label>\n  \u003c/div>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"mfil\">\n   \u003cspan id=\"mRgL\">Range\u003c/span>\u003cdiv class=\"seg sm\" id=\"mRg\" role=\"group\" aria-labelledby=\"mRgL\">\u003c/div>\n   \u003cspan class=\"selw\">\u003cselect id=\"mBrand\" aria-label=\"Brand\">\u003c/select>\u003c/span>\n   \u003cspan class=\"selw\">\u003cselect id=\"mSort\" aria-label=\"Sort by\">\u003coption value=\"r\">Longest range\u003c/option>\u003coption value=\"u\">Largest battery\u003c/option>\u003coption value=\"k\">Fastest charging\u003c/option>\u003coption value=\"p\">Lowest price\u003c/option>\u003coption value=\"b\">Brand A–Z\u003c/option>\u003c/select>\u003c/span>\n   \u003clabel class=\"sw2\">\u003cinput id=\"mSoon\" type=\"checkbox\" checked>\u003cspan>Include announced models\u003c/span>\u003c/label>\n  \u003c/div>\n  \u003cp class=\"mcount\" id=\"mCount\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">\u003c/p>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"mgrid\" id=\"mList\">\u003c/div>\u003cp class=\"seo-advice\" id=\"mAdvice\">\u003c/p>\n  \u003cp class=\"mdisc\">These are manufacturer figures. Cold weather and heavy loads reduce range.\u003c/p>\n  \u003caside class=\"ad band\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\">Advertisement\u003c/aside>\n \u003c/div>\n \u003cdiv class=\"mcmp\" id=\"mBar\" hidden>\u003cspan id=\"mBarT\">\u003c/span>\u003cbutton class=\"lnk\" type=\"button\" data-mclear>Clear\u003c/button>\u003cbutton class=\"cta\" type=\"button\" id=\"mGo\">Compare\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\n \u003cdialog class=\"mdlg\" id=\"mDlg\" aria-labelledby=\"mDlgT\">\n  \u003cdiv class=\"mdh\">\u003ch2 id=\"mDlgT\">Compare\u003c/h2>\u003cbutton class=\"wzx\" type=\"button\" data-mclose aria-label=\"Close\">\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/button>\u003c/div>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"mdb\" id=\"mDlgB\">\u003c/div>\n \u003c/dialog>\n\u003c/section>","model":"\u003csection class=\"page\" data-page=\"model\" hidden>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap\">\n  \u003cnav class=\"vcrumb\" id=\"vCrumb\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\u003c/nav>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"phead\">\u003ch1 id=\"vTitle\" tabindex=\"-1\">\u003c/h1>\u003cp class=\"seo-intro\" id=\"vIntro\">\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\n  \u003cdiv id=\"vBody\">\u003c/div>\n \u003c/div>\n\u003c/section>","zone":"\u003csection class=\"page\" data-page=\"zone\" hidden>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap zwr\" data-no-translate>\n  \u003cnav class=\"vcrumb\" id=\"zCrumb\" aria-label=\"Kruimelpad\">\u003c/nav>\n  \u003carticle class=\"ga zga\" id=\"zArt\">\u003c/article>\n \u003c/div>\n\u003c/section>","faq":"\u003csection class=\"page\" data-page=\"faq\" hidden>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap\">\n  \u003cdiv class=\"phead\">\u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Switching to electric: costs, charging and rules\u003c/h1>\u003cp class=\"seo-intro\">From one electric van to an entire fleet: start with costs and daily operations. Use these guides to assess charging, range, grants and access to zero-emission zones.\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\n  \u003col class=\"gtl\" id=\"gTl\">\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/checklist/\">\u003csmall>01\u003c/small>\u003cb>Step-by-step plan\u003c/b>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/grid-capacity/\">\u003csmall>02\u003c/small>\u003cb>Grid congestion and your connection\u003c/b>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/charging/\">\u003csmall>03\u003c/small>\u003cb>Depot and en-route charging\u003c/b>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/electricity-and-solar/\">\u003csmall>04\u003c/small>\u003cb>Electricity contracts and solar\u003c/b>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/range-planning/\">\u003csmall>05\u003c/small>\u003cb>Range and route planning\u003c/b>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/zero-emission-zones/\">\u003csmall>06\u003c/small>\u003cb>Zero-emission zones\u003c/b>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/grants/\">\u003csmall>07\u003c/small>\u003cb>Grants and tax schemes\u003c/b>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/truck-toll/\">\u003csmall>08\u003c/small>\u003cb>Truck toll and foreign tolls\u003c/b>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/buy-lease-or-rent/\">\u003csmall>09\u003c/small>\u003cb>Buy or lease\u003c/b>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/battery-and-residual-value/\">\u003csmall>10\u003c/small>\u003cb>Battery, warranty and residual value\u003c/b>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/licences-and-workshop/\">\u003csmall>11\u003c/small>\u003cb>Licences, weight and workshops\u003c/b>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/glossary/\">\u003csmall>12\u003c/small>\u003cb>Glossary\u003c/b>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003c/ol>\n  \u003ch2 class=\"gfh\" id=\"vragen\">FAQs\u003c/h2>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"faqw\">\n   \u003caside class=\"rail\">\n    \u003cnav aria-label=\"Onderwerpen\">\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-jump=\"fq1\">The calculation\u003c/button>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-jump=\"fq5\">Switching to electric\u003c/button>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-jump=\"fq2\">Grants and tax\u003c/button>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-jump=\"fq3\">Charging and tolls\u003c/button>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" data-jump=\"fq4\">Your data\u003c/button>\u003c/nav>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"ad\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\">Advertisement\u003c/div>\n   \u003c/aside>\n   \u003cdiv class=\"faq\">\n    \u003csection id=\"fq1\">\u003ch2>The calculation\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Which vehicles can I compare?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Tractor units, rigid trucks, vans and buses. Each category starts with suitable example figures that you replace with your own. Truck toll and AanZET apply only to trucks, so they are excluded for vans and buses.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>What does total cost mean?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>All costs over the time you use a vehicle, not just its purchase price. This shows whether lower energy, maintenance and toll costs offset the higher purchase price of an electric vehicle.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Can I include finance, charging and tolls?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Yes. Choose finance under Purchase: your own money or a finance lease, with down payment, interest and a final balloon payment. Under Additional costs, the last step of the form, include a depot charger, en-route charging and, for trucks, foreign tolls. Each item can be enabled separately. With all items off, only the core costs are calculated.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Can I lease as well?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Yes, in two ways. Choose a finance lease under Purchase, at How you pay; it is on by default for tractor units and rigid trucks. You remain the economic owner, so AanZET, MIA and KIA apply to you. Choose an operating lease per side under Purchase: a monthly lease price then replaces purchase, residual value and interest. The leasing company applies for AanZET; with an operating lease you do not get MIA. Without a quote we estimate the lease price; enter your own quote and we use your contract mileage and excess-mileage rate. The detailed results also show what a finance lease would cost.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>How reliable is the result?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Results depend on your inputs. Example figures vary by make, configuration and use. Driver costs, overheads and VAT are excluded; finance is included only if you choose a finance or operating lease under Purchase. Use this as an initial comparison, not financial or tax advice.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>How do you calculate range?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Range is usable battery capacity divided by energy consumption per kilometre. Cold weather and heavy loads reduce it; the winter estimate is about 25% lower. Daily distance is annual mileage divided by operating days. If daily distance exceeds range, enable En-route charging under Additional costs.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>At what annual mileage is electric cheaper?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>See Electric is cheaper from below the result. We hold your other figures constant and find the annual mileage at which electric has lower annual costs than diesel. The share of kilometres subject to truck toll stays the same.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Why is residual value excluded from payback?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Payback is the point at which cumulative electric-vehicle costs (the additional investment plus annual operating costs) fall below diesel costs. Finance is excluded, because the investment itself is already counted; adding interest would count it twice. Residual value is received at sale, so it is excluded from payback too. It is included in annual and per-kilometre costs through depreciation.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n    \u003c/section>\n    \u003csection id=\"fq5\">\u003ch2>Switching to electric\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Which electric vehicles are available?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>The \u003ca href=\"/en/models/\">Vehicles\u003c/a> models page lists electric tractor units, rigid trucks, vans and buses, including upcoming models such as the Tesla Semi. View batteries, range and charging power, compare up to three models, and choose Calculate with this model to load battery, consumption and price into your calculation.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>What are zero-emission zones?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Since 1 January 2025, more Dutch municipalities have introduced zero-emission zones for urban logistics. Vans and trucks newly registered from 2025 must be zero-emission to enter. Older vehicles have transition periods by Euro class. See \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/zero-emission-zones/\">Zero-emission zones\u003c/a> shows how long your vehicle can still enter these zones.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Can I charge at my depot?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Usually, but fast charging or several vehicles may need more grid capacity. Many regions face congestion and waiting lists. Check the Netbeheer Nederland map early, contact your grid operator and discuss storage, smart charging or flexible contracts. For a map and power check, see \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/grid-capacity/\">Grid congestion\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>How long does charging take?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Depot charging usually takes place overnight: a 50 kW charger takes about 11 hours to charge a 540 kWh battery. A 350 kW fast charger can add substantial energy during a break. Charging during mandatory driver breaks minimises downtime. Calculate it under \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/charging/\">Charging\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>What happens to the battery as it ages?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Battery capacity gradually falls, especially with frequent fast charging and extreme temperatures. Ask about warranty duration, minimum guaranteed capacity and a battery health report. Battery condition strongly affects residual value. See \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/battery-and-residual-value/\">Battery, warranty and residual value\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>What changes for drivers and route planning?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Electric vehicles are quieter, vibrate less and accelerate smoothly. Plan charging into the schedule, ideally at your depot and during breaks. In winter, preheat while plugged in to protect driving range.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n    \u003c/section>\n    \u003csection id=\"fq2\">\u003ch2>Grants and tax\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>How is the AanZET grant calculated?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>AanZET is a capped percentage of the chassis price of a new zero-emission truck, excluding bodywork and VAT. Rates depend on company size and category: N3 (over 12 tonnes), or N2 from 10,000 kg. In 2026, rates are 11.1–29% for N3 and 6.1–14.8% for N2. Applications run in funding rounds with limited budgets. Check RVO for an open round. See \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/grants/\">Grants and tax schemes\u003c/a> explains which rules apply to you.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>What is MIA and why can&#39;t I combine it with AanZET?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>MIA is a Dutch tax allowance for environmental investments. This calculator uses a qualifying amount of 90% of the purchase price and an additional deduction of 36%. The indicative net tax benefit uses corporation tax rates of 19% up to €200,000 profit and 25.8% above that. MIA cannot be combined with AanZET. Check current terms with RVO and the Dutch Tax Administration.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Are grants available for electric vans or buses?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>The national SEBA grant for electric vans has ended, and AanZET covers trucks only. A new electric coach can get STour or otherwise MIA; choose them under Bus. For a van the benefit is mainly fiscal: the KIA small-business allowance, and an electric van pays no BPM registration tax while a new diesel van does. If you receive other support, such as a municipal or provincial grant, enter a custom amount under grants.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>What is ERE revenue?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Charging electric vehicles can earn Dutch emission reduction units (EREs), which can be sold. Net revenue per kWh is a market assumption and can change. Enter the rate available to your business.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n    \u003c/section>\n    \u003csection id=\"fq3\">\u003ch2>Charging and tolls\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>How does the truck toll affect the calculation?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Since 1 July 2026, N2 and N3 trucks over 3,500 kg pay a distance-based toll on almost all Dutch motorways and selected provincial and municipal roads. Electric trucks pay much less. Buses and standard vans are excluded. Enter your toll-road mileage and rate. Check current rates at vrachtwagenheffing.nl. See also \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/truck-toll/\">Truck toll and foreign tolls\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>How do you account for a charger?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Enable a depot charger under Additional costs. The example uses one installed 50 kW charger. Investment after SPRILA support is spread over the depreciation period, with grid connection, maintenance and standing charges added. For a 50 kW DC charger, SPRILA offers €9,760 for SMEs or €4,880 for larger companies, capped at 40% or 20% of the installed charger cost respectively and subject to a €2,500 minimum grant.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n    \u003c/section>\n    \u003csection id=\"fq4\">\u003ch2>Your data\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Do you store my data?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Your inputs are saved in your browser so you can continue later. Reset example figures restores the defaults. With analytics consent, we measure calculator use without names or contact details. Change your choice using Cookies in the footer. Read more in the \u003ca href=\"/en/privacy/\">privacy policy\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Can I share or save the result?\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Yes. Share copies a short summary and a link containing your exact calculation, for a colleague or accountant. The recipient sees the same figures. PDF lets you save or print the result. Compare places two calculations side by side.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n    \u003c/section>\n   \u003c/div>\n  \u003c/div>\n \u003c/div>\n\u003c/section>","gids":"\u003csection class=\"page\" data-page=\"gids\" hidden>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap\">\n  \u003cdiv class=\"gw\">\n   \u003cdiv class=\"gm\">\n    \u003ca class=\"gbk\" href=\"/en/switching-guide/\">Switching guide\u003c/a>\n\n    \u003carticle class=\"ga\" data-g=\"stappenplan\" hidden>\n     \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Electrify your fleet: a practical step-by-step plan\u003c/h1>\n     \u003cp class=\"glead\">First establish which routes can go electric and whether charging is feasible at your site. Then compare costs and choose a replacement date for each vehicle. These nine steps align investment with operations.\u003c/p>\n     \u003col class=\"gst\" id=\"gSt\">\u003cli>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"gck\" data-gst=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\" aria-label=\"Map your routes\">\u003c/button>\u003cdiv>\u003cb>Map your routes\u003c/b>\u003cp>Record daily distances, downtime and overnight parking. This determines the battery capacity and charging power you need.\u003c/p>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/range-planning/\">Range and route planning\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"gck\" data-gst=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\" aria-label=\"Check your grid connection\">\u003c/button>\u003cdiv>\u003cb>Check your grid connection\u003c/b>\u003cp>Start here: upgrading a connection in a congested area can take years.\u003c/p>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/grid-capacity/\">Grid congestion\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"gck\" data-gst=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"false\" aria-label=\"Calculate the costs\">\u003c/button>\u003cdiv>\u003cb>Calculate the costs\u003c/b>\u003cp>Use your own mileage, prices and grants, and compare with your current diesel.\u003c/p>\u003ca href=\"/en/\">Open the calculator\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"gck\" data-gst=\"3\" aria-pressed=\"false\" aria-label=\"Choose a vehicle\">\u003c/button>\u003cdiv>\u003cb>Choose a vehicle\u003c/b>\u003cp>Check usable battery capacity, charging power and lead time. Test-drive on your own routes.\u003c/p>\u003ca href=\"/en/models/\">Vehicles\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"gck\" data-gst=\"4\" aria-pressed=\"false\" aria-label=\"Apply for grants in time\">\u003c/button>\u003cdiv>\u003cb>Apply for grants in time\u003c/b>\u003cp>Check the application deadlines for AanZET and SPRILA, and register your MIA investment within three months.\u003c/p>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/grants/\">Grants and tax schemes\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"gck\" data-gst=\"5\" aria-pressed=\"false\" aria-label=\"Arrange charging\">\u003c/button>\u003cdiv>\u003cb>Arrange charging\u003c/b>\u003cp>Arrange depot chargers, a charging card for the road and a certified meter for ERE revenue.\u003c/p>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/charging/\">Charging\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"gck\" data-gst=\"6\" aria-pressed=\"false\" aria-label=\"Choose between buying and leasing\">\u003c/button>\u003cdiv>\u003cb>Choose between buying and leasing\u003c/b>\u003cp>Compare monthly costs and who carries residual-value risk.\u003c/p>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/buy-lease-or-rent/\">Buy or lease\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"gck\" data-gst=\"7\" aria-pressed=\"false\" aria-label=\"Prepare drivers and workshop\">\u003c/button>\u003cdiv>\u003cb>Prepare drivers and workshop\u003c/b>\u003cp>Check driving licences, training, NEN 9140 workshop requirements and your insurer’s conditions.\u003c/p>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/licences-and-workshop/\">Licences, weight and workshops\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"gck\" data-gst=\"8\" aria-pressed=\"false\" aria-label=\"Measure and adjust\">\u003c/button>\u003cdiv>\u003cb>Measure and adjust\u003c/b>\u003cp>Track consumption, charging costs and battery health to inform your next purchase and help resale.\u003c/p>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/battery-and-residual-value/\">Battery and residual value\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/li>\u003c/ol>\n    \u003ch2>When should you replace each vehicle?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Compare lease expiry, expected maintenance costs and customer access with vehicle and charger lead times. Calculate both replacement now and keeping the current vehicle. A phased transition may fit your budget and charging capacity better than replacing everything at once.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp class=\"gcl\">Multiple vehicles or sites? \u003ca href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\">Have a fleet analysis made\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\n\u003c/article>\n\n    \u003carticle class=\"ga\" data-g=\"netcongestie\" hidden>\n     \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Electric charging with grid congestion: what can your connection support?\u003c/h1>\n     \u003cp class=\"glead\">Ordering an electric vehicle is one step; being able to charge on time is the next. Compare daily charging needs with available power, building demand and parking hours. The map is an initial indication; your grid operator confirms site-specific capacity.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtool\" id=\"gtMap\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>How much power do you need?\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>Small-user connections go up to 3×80 A, roughly 55 kW. Above this you need a large-user connection. Since 1 July 2026, small and large applications in congested areas share one waiting list. Making better use of your existing capacity reduces dependence on it.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtool\" id=\"gtKw\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>What you can do\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gop\">\n      \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Smart charging\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Charging management spreads demand through the night and accounts for your building’s consumption to stay within capacity. It is often the cheapest first step and sufficient for several vehicles.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n      \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Stay within your current grid connection\u003c/summary>\u003cp>If charging fits within your existing connection, you avoid the waiting list. Smart charging and longer charging windows often allow more vehicles than expected. Use the calculation above.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n      \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Depot battery storage\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Battery storage charges when grid capacity is available and supplies extra power when vehicles charge. It covers peaks without a larger connection and can increase use of your own solar generation.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n      \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Flexible grid contract\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Grid operators offer contracts allowing higher demand outside busy hours, restricting supply for a set number of hours annually, or reducing supply during congestion (non-firm). These can suit overnight charging, be available sooner and cost less.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n      \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Work with neighbouring businesses\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Businesses on an industrial estate can form an energy hub, sharing grid capacity through a group contract and coordinating demand: one charges overnight while another operates during the day.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n      \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Charge at customers or en route\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Charge while unloading at customers or at motorway hubs. Electricity costs more per kWh, but can bridge the wait for your own connection. See \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/charging/\">Charging\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n      \u003cdetails>\u003csummary>Bridge the waiting period\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Until your connection is ready, you can temporarily use a mobile battery or charging unit. Ask your dealer or charger supplier; some offer this alongside the vehicle purchase.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\n     \u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>How to apply\u003c/h2>\n     \u003col class=\"gnum\">\n      \u003cli>\u003cb>Check your address\u003c/b> on the grid capacity map to see whether power is available and whether there is a waiting list.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>\u003cb>Calculate the power\u003c/b> you need for your fleet today and in five years.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>\u003cb>Enquire\u003c/b>: up to 3×80 A through Mijnaansluiting.nl; larger connections directly through your grid operator. Applications are queued, with priority for social functions and projects that relieve the grid. Apply before the vehicle arrives.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>\u003cb>Ask about alternatives\u003c/b>: flexible contracts, expected waiting times and what is possible in the meantime.\u003c/li>\n     \u003c/ol>\n     \u003ch2>From energy needs to a charging plan\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Multiply daily distance by energy use per km. Divide the energy needed by available charging hours and allow for charging losses and simultaneous demand. Check contracted capacity as well as the physical connection.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"glk\">\n      \u003ca href=\"https://capaciteitskaart.netbeheernederland.nl/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Netbeheer Nederland grid capacity map\u003c/a>\n      \u003ca href=\"https://www.mijnaansluiting.nl/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Apply for a grid connection or upgrade (Mijnaansluiting.nl)\u003c/a>\n      \u003ca href=\"https://rvo.nl/sites/default/files/2024-07/Factsheets-oplossingen-netcongestie-bedrijven-versie-2.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Grid congestion guidance (RVO)\u003c/a>\n     \u003c/div>\n     \u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/detailed-calculation/\">Include a charger and grid connection under Additional costs\u003c/a>\n\n\u003cp class=\"gcl\">Multiple vehicles or sites? \u003ca href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\">Request fleet advice\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\n\u003c/article>\n\n    \u003carticle class=\"ga\" data-g=\"laden\" hidden>\n     \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Charging an electric truck or van: power and costs\u003c/h1>\n     \u003cp class=\"glead\">A charger costs more than the hardware alone. Include installation, civil works, connection, management and electricity. Choose charging power based on daily energy needs and the time available to charge.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtool\" id=\"gtLd\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>At your depot\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>Charging op je Depot is het goedkoopst: je betaalt je own Electricity price and ontvangt zelf de ERE revenue. For a van, an \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/glossary/#begrip-acdc\">AC\u003c/a> charge point of 11 or 22 kW is usually enough. For a truck, a \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/glossary/#begrip-acdc\">DC\u003c/a> charger of 40 to 50 kW per vehicle is the obvious choice, or a faster charger shared across vehicles with load management.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cp>Choose a charge point with a certified meter to register ERE revenue. SPRILA supports chargers for your own commercial vehicles.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>En route\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>More truck charging hubs with 350 kW and higher power are opening on major corridors. Charge during the mandatory 45-minute break after 4.5 hours of driving to minimise downtime. Public charging costs more per kWh, but an operator’s business contract may beat ad-hoc charging-card rates.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Charging while loading and unloading\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>If the truck is standing still at a customer or distribution centre to load or unload anyway, it can top up during that time. That is called opportunity charging: no separate stop and no extra waiting time for the driver. Even a modest charger at the dock adds enough in an hour of loading and unloading for tens of kilometres.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Megawatt charging\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>The Megawatt Charging System (\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/glossary/#begrip-mcs\">MCS\u003c/a>) is the new connector for heavy trucks, with a charging speed of over 1 MW. The first trucks and charge points are available. Ask when buying whether the vehicle has MCS or can be fitted with it, as it determines how much you can charge during a break.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>What does a truck or van charger cost?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Request a quote for the complete site, including cabling, protection, grid upgrades and service. Spread investment over expected usage and compare depot with en-route charging. Higher utilisation can reduce charging costs per vehicle.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"glk\">\n      \u003ca href=\"https://ondernemersplein.overheid.nl/subsidies-en-regelingen/sprila/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SPRILA charger grant\u003c/a>\n      \u003ca href=\"https://www.rvo.nl/nieuws/brandstoftransitieverplichting-verdien-met-laden\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Earn revenue from charging: EREs (RVO)\u003c/a>\n      \u003ca href=\"https://openchargemap.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Find charge points (Open Charge Map)\u003c/a>\n     \u003c/div>\n     \u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/detailed-calculation/\">Include depot, en-route and smart charging under Additional costs\u003c/a>\n\n\u003cp class=\"gcl\">Multiple vehicles or sites? \u003ca href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\">Fleet advice for your entire fleet\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\n\u003c/article>\n\n    \u003carticle class=\"ga\" data-g=\"stroom\" hidden>\n     \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Charging cost per km: tariffs, solar and smart charging\u003c/h1>\n     \u003cp class=\"glead\">A low electricity price helps, but compare the full tariff and actual charging times. Assess how fixed, variable or dynamic tariffs and solar fit your vehicle operations.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtool\" id=\"gtEn\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>What you pay per kWh\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>Your electricity price includes supply, energy tax and grid charges. Energy tax per kWh decreases with higher consumption, so adding electric vehicles often lowers the average rate. Businesses can reclaim VAT.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cp>With a large-user grid connection, charges also depend on your highest monthly power demand. Spreading charging through the night reduces peaks and costs.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Fixed, variable or dynamic\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cul class=\"gli\">\n      \u003cli>\u003cb>Fixed\u003c/b>: the same price per kWh throughout the contract. Predictable, but you do not benefit from cheap hours.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>\u003cb>Variable\u003c/b>: the supplier changes the price a few times a year.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>\u003cb>Dynamic\u003c/b>: hourly pricing linked to the electricity market. Overnight and sunny-afternoon charging can be cheaper. Charge points must support price-based scheduling.\u003c/li>\n     \u003c/ul>\n     \u003ch2>Rooftop solar\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>One \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/glossary/#begrip-eenheden\">kWp\u003c/a>  of solar panels produces about 900 kWh a year on average in the Netherlands. Zonnestroom die Immediate in je Vehicles gaat, is de goedkoopste Electricity die er is. Maar de zon schijnt overdag and vrachtwagens Charging vaak &#39;s nachts: met One batterij or bijladen tijdens de middagpauze gaat er meer zon in je Vehicles. Teruggeleverde Electricity levert steeds minder op and kost At veel leveranciers geld.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Use your actual charging costs\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Use the split between depot and public charging, including losses and fixed costs. Do not automatically treat solar as free: investment and alternative revenue matter too. Test higher electricity prices.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"glk\">\n      \u003ca href=\"https://re.jrc.ec.europa.eu/pvg_tools/nl/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Estimate rooftop solar generation (PVGIS)\u003c/a>\n      \u003ca href=\"https://www.rvo.nl/nieuws/brandstoftransitieverplichting-verdien-met-laden\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Earn revenue from charging: EREs (RVO)\u003c/a>\n     \u003c/div>\n     \u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/detailed-calculation/\">Enable smart charging and solar under Additional costs\u003c/a>\n\n\u003cp class=\"gcl\">Multiple vehicles or sites? \u003ca href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\">Request fleet advice\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\n\u003c/article>\n\n    \u003carticle class=\"ga\" data-g=\"actieradius\" hidden>\n     \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Real-world electric van and truck range\u003c/h1>\n     \u003cp class=\"glead\">The largest advertised range is not automatically the best choice. Check long working days, payload, towing and winter routes. Establish where you arrive with sufficient reserve and which charging stops fit the schedule.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtool\" id=\"gtAr\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>How far do they really go?\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>The figures below are the manufacturer figures for all 67 vehicles in our comparison. In practice you rarely get the full value: in winter and with heavy work, count on 20 to 30 percent less, and plan your daily route for the worst day rather than the best.\u003c/p> \u003cp>Terms such as WLTP, usable battery capacity and manufacturer figures are explained under \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/glossary/\">Glossary\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtb\">\n      \u003ctable class=\"gtt gwr\">\n       \u003cthead>\n\u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Category\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Smallest range\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Median\u003c/th>\n\u003cth>Largest range\u003c/th>\n\u003c/tr>\n\u003c/thead>\n       \u003ctbody>\n        \u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Tractor units\u003c/th>\n\u003ctd>450 km\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>550 km\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>700 km\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Rigid trucks\u003c/th>\n\u003ctd>200 km\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>400 km\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>600 km\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Vans\u003c/th>\n\u003ctd>227 km\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>350 km\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>470 km\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\n\u003cth>Buses\u003c/th>\n\u003ctd>310 km\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>500 km\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd>600 km\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>\n       \u003c/tbody>\n      \u003c/table>\n     \u003c/div>\n     \u003cp>The longest range among tractor units is currently the Volvo FH Aero Electric (700 km), followed by the Renault Trucks E-Tech T 780 (660 km) and the Iveco S-eWay (600 km).\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Electric van with the longest range\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>Of the electric vans available now, the Volkswagen ID. Buzz Cargo goes furthest: 459 kilometres on one charge (manufacturer figure). Next are the large models such as the Opel Movano Electric at 430 kilometres. The upcoming new Renault Trafic Van E-Tech promises 470 kilometres.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/models/vans/\">See all electric vans by range\u003c/a>\n     \u003ch2>What affects consumption\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>Weight and speed have the greatest effect. Driving at 80 instead of 90 km/h can save around 10%. Winter cab and battery heating, refrigeration and electrically powered cranes add consumption. Motorway use consumes more than urban driving, where braking recovers energy.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Plan around charging\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cul class=\"gli\">\n      \u003cli>Start with the best-fitting routes: regular journeys that return to your depot every evening.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>Plan charging during breaks and customer stops.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>Preheat or cool the vehicle while plugged in to protect range.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>Allow 10–20% charge on arrival, especially in winter.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>Test the vehicle on your own routes first. Many dealers offer a demo or trial period.\u003c/li>\n     \u003c/ul>\n     \u003ch2>Payload and towing: does the vehicle fit your work?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Check cargo volume, usable payload and permitted towing weight for the exact configuration. Battery, bodywork, occupants and tools all affect weight. Request a test with a representative load; catalogue figures do not replace real-world testing.\u003c/p>\n\u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/models/\">Compare vehicles by range\u003c/a>\n\n\u003cp class=\"gcl\">Multiple vehicles or sites? \u003ca href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\">Request fleet advice\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\n\u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/\">Calculate your costs: diesel or electric\u003c/a>\n\u003c/article>\n\n    \u003carticle class=\"ga\" data-g=\"zero-emissiezones\" hidden>\n     \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Zero-emission zones: can your van or truck enter the city?\u003c/h1>\n     \u003cp class=\"glead\">Check access by registration, municipality and travel date. A low-emission zone differs from a zero-emission zone. Vehicle category, emissions class, first registration and any exemption determine access.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtool\" id=\"gtZm\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>Can your diesel still enter?\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtool\" id=\"gtZe\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>Transition rules\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtb\">\n      \u003ctable class=\"gtt gwr\">\n       \u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Diesel\u003c/th>\u003cth>Year of manufacture\u003c/th>\u003cth>Zone access until\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\n       \u003ctbody>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>Euro 5 van\u003c/th>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>1 January 2027\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>Euro 6 van\u003c/th>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>1 January 2028, extension to 2029 proposed\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>Euro VI rigid truck\u003c/th>\u003ctd>2017–2019\u003c/td>\u003ctd>1 January 2028\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>Euro VI rigid truck\u003c/th>\u003ctd>2020–2024\u003c/td>\u003ctd>1 January 2030\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>Euro VI tractor unit\u003c/th>\u003ctd>2017–2024\u003c/td>\u003ctd>1 January 2030\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>Lower Euro class\u003c/th>\u003ctd>\u003c/td>\u003ctd>No access\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n       \u003c/tbody>\n      \u003c/table>\n     \u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>Good to know\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cul class=\"gli\">\n      \u003cli>The rules are national, but each municipality decides whether and when to introduce a zone and how large it is.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>Plug-in hybrid trucks can receive an exemption until 1 January 2030 if they demonstrably operate electrically within the zone.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>Municipalities offer exemptions, such as day permits or exemptions for special-purpose vehicles.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>Enter your current diesel registration in the calculator to see zone access deadlines and when switching could offer the greatest benefit.\u003c/li>\n     \u003c/ul>\n     \u003ch2>Start with the municipality and registration check\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Use the official registration check and verify boundaries and start dates with the relevant municipality. Distinguish current rules from announced changes in your replacement plan. A proposed extension does not confirm access.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"glk\">\n      \u003ca href=\"https://opwegnaarzes.nl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Registration check and zone map (Op weg naar ZES)\u003c/a>\n     \u003c/div>\n     \u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/\">Compare your current diesel in the calculator\u003c/a>\n\n\u003cp class=\"gcl\">Multiple vehicles or sites? \u003ca href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\">Request fleet advice\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\n\u003c/article>\n\n    \u003carticle class=\"ga\" data-g=\"subsidies\" hidden>\n     \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Grants for electric trucks and chargers\u003c/h1>\n     \u003cp class=\"glead\">AanZET supports new zero-emission trucks; SPRILA and SPULA cover different charging infrastructure. Eligibility depends on vehicle, site and application timing. Also calculate without grants to understand the investment dependency.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtool\" id=\"gtSb\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>How much grant do you get with AanZET?\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtb\">\n      \u003ctable class=\"gtt gwr\">\n       \u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Company\u003c/th>\u003cth>Tractor unit or N3 rigid truck\u003c/th>\u003cth>N2 rigid truck from 10 tonnes\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\n       \u003ctbody>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>Small or non-profit\u003c/th>\u003ctd>29%, max. € 115,200\u003c/td>\u003ctd>14.8%, max. € 36,900\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>Medium\u003c/th>\u003ctd>21%, max. € 83,200\u003c/td>\u003ctd>12%, max. € 29,900\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>Large\u003c/th>\u003ctd>11.1%, max. € 43,900\u003c/td>\u003ctd>6.1%, max. € 15,200\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n       \u003c/tbody>\n      \u003c/table>\n     \u003c/div>\n     \u003cp>As of 30 October 2026, AanZET is temporarily closed. RVO expects the next round around mid-March 2027; check the confirmed date and terms before ordering.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>MIA as an alternative\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>For an electric truck under code D 3116 in 2026, the MIA deduction is 36% of 90% of the eligible investment amount, with no Vamil allowance. Your benefit depends on your tax rate and tax position. AanZET and MIA cannot be combined for the same investment.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Buses and coaches: STour or MIA\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>A new electric coach (M2 or M3, approved for 100 km/h) can get STour: 60% of the extra cost over a comparable diesel for a small company, 50% for medium and 30% for large, up to €180,000, €150,000 or €90,000. Applications are open in 2026 until 30 November, while budget lasts. Alternatively you can use MIA (code A 3108): 36% on 90% of the price, with Vamil. STour and MIA cannot be combined for the same coach.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Vans: no grant, but tax benefits\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>There is no longer a national grant for electric vans, and they are not on the 2026 Milieulijst. An electric van pays no BPM registration tax, while a new diesel van has paid BPM based on its CO₂ emissions since 2025. The KIA small-business allowance may also apply, to diesel and electric alike.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Check the application timing\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cul class=\"gli\">\n      \u003cli>AanZET has funding rounds with limited budgets. Read the application timing rules before signing a purchase or lease agreement: signing too early can make you ineligible.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>Register MIA within three months of committing to the investment, usually from the order date.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>AanZET and MIA cannot be combined for the same vehicle. Compare which gives you the greater benefit.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>Application timing also matters for SPRILA. Check the terms before ordering chargers.\u003c/li>\n     \u003c/ul>\n     \u003ch2>SPRILA or SPULA: what type of charging site are you building?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>SPRILA covers private business charging infrastructure; SPULA covers publicly accessible heavy-vehicle charging sites. Check current availability, site requirements and application timing with RVO before making commitments.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"glk\">\n      \u003ca href=\"https://www.rvo.nl/subsidies-financiering/aanzet\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AanZET (RVO)\u003c/a>\n      \u003ca href=\"https://www.rvo.nl/subsidies-financiering/aanzet/voorwaarden\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AanZET eligibility and conditions\u003c/a>\n      \u003ca href=\"https://www.rvo.nl/subsidies-financiering/mia-vamil/ondernemers/mobiliteit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MIA for mobility investments (RVO)\u003c/a>\n      \u003ca href=\"https://www.rvo.nl/subsidies-financiering/stour\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">STour (RVO)\u003c/a>\n      \u003ca href=\"https://www.rvo.nl/subsidies-financiering/laadinfrastructuur/sprila-aanschaf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SPRILA (RVO)\u003c/a>\u003ca href=\"https://www.rvo.nl/subsidies-financiering/laadinfrastructuur/spula\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SPULA (RVO)\u003c/a>\n      \u003ca href=\"https://www.rvo.nl/nieuws/brandstoftransitieverplichting-verdien-met-laden\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">EREs: earning revenue from charging (RVO)\u003c/a>\n     \u003c/div>\n     \u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/\">Include grants in your calculation\u003c/a>\n\n\u003cp class=\"gcl\">Multiple vehicles or sites? \u003ca href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\">Request fleet advice\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\n\u003c/article>\n\n    \u003carticle class=\"ga\" data-g=\"heffing\" hidden>\n     \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Truck toll: cost per km for diesel and electric\u003c/h1>\n     \u003cp class=\"glead\">The truck toll changes the comparison between diesel and electric trucks. Use chargeable mileage on your own routes and the correct weight and CO₂ class. The rate alone does not determine annual costs.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtool\" id=\"gtHf\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>How it works\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>Rates depend on weight, CO₂ class and Euro emissions class. All rates are temporarily 22.3% lower from 1 September to 31 December 2026. The calculator uses the 2027 rates: diesel Euro VI in CO₂ class 1 and electric in CO₂ class 5. Buses and vans up to 3,500 kg are excluded.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Rate per kilometre in 2027\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtb\">\n      \u003ctable class=\"gtt gwr\">\n       \u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Maximum mass\u003c/th>\u003cth>Diesel Euro VI\u003c/th>\u003cth>Electric\u003c/th>\u003cth>Difference per 10,000 km\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\n       \u003ctbody>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>3.5 to 12 tonnes\u003c/th>\u003ctd>€ 0.116\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0.026\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 900\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>12 to 18 tonnes\u003c/th>\u003ctd>€ 0.165\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0.036\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 1,290\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>18 to 32 tonnes\u003c/th>\u003ctd>€ 0.187\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0.037\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 1,500\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>Over 32 tonnes\u003c/th>\u003ctd>€ 0.206\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0.040\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 1,660\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n       \u003c/tbody>\n      \u003c/table>\n     \u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>Which roads charge the truck toll?\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>The toll applies on almost all motorways and on some provincial and municipal roads, mainly where traffic would otherwise divert to avoid it. If a trip runs entirely on roads without the toll, you pay nothing for those kilometres.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>How is the toll enforced?\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>Every truck needs an on-board unit from an approved provider. The unit records where you drive by satellite and settles the kilometres. Roadside checks use the number plate to verify an active unit is present; without a working unit, a fine follows.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>What does the toll cost per year?\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>Worked example: a tractor unit over 32 tonnes driving 100,000 kilometres a year on tolled roads pays € 20,100 a year in truck toll as a diesel. Electric, that is € 3,800. The difference of € 16,300 a year comes on top of the difference in fuel and maintenance costs.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Abroad\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>Electric can also reduce tolls abroad, but the benefit varies by country. The per-kilometre rates used are shown below.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtb\" id=\"gtTol\">\u003ctable class=\"gtt\">\u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>\u003c/th>\u003cth>Diesel\u003c/th>\u003cth>Electric\u003c/th>\u003cth>Per 10.000 km\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\u003ctbody>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Flanders\u003c/th>\u003ctd>€ 0,286\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0.038\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 2.480\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Wallonia\u003c/th>\u003ctd>€ 0,205\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0,205\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003cth>France\u003c/th>\u003ctd>€ 0,300\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0,300\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Germany\u003c/th>\u003ctd>€ 0,348\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0,000\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 3.480\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Italy\u003c/th>\u003ctd>€ 0,200\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0,200\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Poland\u003c/th>\u003ctd>€ 0,130\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0,130\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003ctr>\u003cth>Austria\u003c/th>\u003ctd>€ 0,572\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 0,119\u003c/td>\u003ctd>€ 4.530\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\u003c/tbody>\u003c/table>\u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>How does the truck toll affect total costs?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Compare tolls alongside depreciation, energy, maintenance and finance. Separate Dutch and foreign mileage and check rate changes during ownership. A lower toll rate does not automatically justify a higher purchase price.\u003c/p>\n\u003cdiv class=\"glk\">\n      \u003ca href=\"https://zoek.officielebekendmakingen.nl/stcrt-2026-18058.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Dutch truck toll rates (government gazette)\u003c/a>\n     \u003c/div>\n     \u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/detailed-calculation/\">Include foreign tolls under Additional costs\u003c/a>\n\n\u003cp class=\"gcl\">Multiple vehicles or sites? \u003ca href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\">Request fleet advice\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\n\u003c/article>\n\n    \u003carticle class=\"ga\" data-g=\"financiering\" hidden>\n     \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Buy or lease an electric commercial vehicle: compare costs\u003c/h1>\n     \u003cp class=\"glead\">Compare purchase, finance lease and operating lease over the same term and mileage. Look beyond monthly payments: deposits, maintenance, insurance, excess mileage and residual risk determine actual costs.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtool\" id=\"gtFn\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>Compare the options\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtb\">\n      \u003ctable class=\"gtt\">\n       \u003cthead>\u003ctr>\u003cth>\u003c/th>\u003cth>Owner\u003c/th>\u003cth>Residual-value risk\u003c/th>\u003cth>Grant\u003c/th>\u003c/tr>\u003c/thead>\n       \u003ctbody>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>Buy\u003c/th>\u003ctd>You\u003c/td>\u003ctd>You\u003c/td>\u003ctd>AanZET or MIA, plus KIA\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>Finance lease\u003c/th>\u003ctd>You, as economic owner\u003c/td>\u003ctd>You\u003c/td>\u003ctd>AanZET or MIA, plus KIA\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n        \u003ctr>\u003cth>Operating lease\u003c/th>\u003ctd>Leasing company\u003c/td>\u003ctd>Leasing company\u003c/td>\u003ctd>AanZET via the leasing company, no MIA or KIA\u003c/td>\u003c/tr>\n       \u003c/tbody>\n      \u003c/table>\n     \u003c/div>\n     \u003cp>Operating lease can be attractive while the used electric-vehicle market develops: the lessor carries residual-value risk.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cp>A finance lease is the most common form for trucks: you spread the payment, with a balloon payment at the end, and keep the grant yourself. With a finance lease you pay VAT on the full price at the start; with an operating lease monthly. In the calculator, choose how you pay under Purchase: your own money or a finance lease, and an operating lease per side. You also see up to which lease price an operating lease beats a finance lease.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Compare quotes on consistent assumptions\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Check what the rate includes and what you pay separately. Confirm the balloon payment, return conditions, charging provision and replacement transport. Include grants only when the applicant and treatment in your contract are clear.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp class=\"gcl\">Multiple vehicles or sites? \u003ca href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\">Request fleet advice\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\n\u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/\">Calculate your costs: diesel or electric\u003c/a>\n\u003c/article>\n\n    \u003carticle class=\"ga\" data-g=\"accu\" hidden>\n     \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Battery and residual value of an electric commercial vehicle\u003c/h1>\n     \u003cp class=\"glead\">Battery health affects usability and resale value of your electric van or truck. Compare warranty terms for the exact configuration, ask for measurements and test different residual values.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtool\" id=\"gtAc\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>Protect battery health\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cul class=\"gli\">\n      \u003cli>Charge steadily at your depot; fast-charge only when needed.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>Avoid charging to 100% unless needed, and do not leave the vehicle full or empty for long periods, particularly in hot weather.\u003c/li>\n      \u003cli>Preheat the battery while plugged in during winter.\u003c/li>\n     \u003c/ul>\n     \u003ch2>Buying and selling\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>Ask about battery warranty and a readable state-of-health report. A recent report helps sell a used vehicle. Always request one when buying used.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>What does battery health mean for cost per km?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>A lower residual value increases depreciation. Less usable capacity may also require extra charging stops. Assess both effects separately and check who pays for damage or capacity below the warranty threshold.\u003c/p>\n\n\u003cp class=\"gcl\">Multiple vehicles or sites? \u003ca href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\">Request fleet advice\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\n\u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/\">Calculate your costs: diesel or electric\u003c/a>\n\u003c/article>\n\n    \u003carticle class=\"ga\" data-g=\"regels\" hidden>\n     \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Electric van: driving licence, payload and workshop\u003c/h1>\n     \u003cp class=\"glead\">Battery weight can affect payload, driving licences and operations. Check maximum technical mass, permitted load and driver requirements. Discuss maintenance and parking with your workshop and insurer.\u003c/p>\n     \u003cdiv class=\"gtool\" id=\"gtRb\">\u003c/div>\n     \u003ch2>Weight and payload\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>European rules allow zero-emission trucks extra gross vehicle weight for the additional drivetrain weight, up to 2,000 kg. This preserves much of the payload. Compare the payload on the registration document when assessing a quote, not just gross weight.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Drivers\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>Electric vehicles are smoother and quieter, but benefit from anticipatory driving and regenerative braking. A short training course can pay back quickly. In town, take extra care around pedestrians and cyclists who may not hear the vehicle.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Workshop and parking\u003c/h2>\n     \u003cp>High-voltage work requires appropriate NEN 9140 training and insulated tools. Ask your insurer about parking and charging requirements, including distance from buildings and fire detection.\u003c/p>\n     \u003ch2>Check the exact vehicle configuration\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Do not rely on the model name alone. Check registration data, any trailer and the licence required for that combination. Reassess payload after bodywork changes.\u003c/p>\n\u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/models/\">See vehicles and their weight class\u003c/a>\n\n\u003cp class=\"gcl\">Multiple vehicles or sites? \u003ca href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\">Request fleet advice\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\n\u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/\">Calculate your costs: diesel or electric\u003c/a>\n\u003c/article> \u003carticle class=\"ga\" data-g=\"begrippen\" hidden> \u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Glossary\u003c/h1> \u003cp class=\"glead\">Every abbreviation and technical term on this site, explained in plain language.\u003c/p> \u003cul class=\"gli\"> \u003cli>\u003ca href=\"#begrip-wltp\">WLTP\u003c/a>\u003c/li> \u003cli>\u003ca href=\"#begrip-acdc\">AC and DC\u003c/a>\u003c/li> \u003cli>\u003ca href=\"#begrip-mcs\">CCS and MCS\u003c/a>\u003c/li> \u003cli>\u003ca href=\"#begrip-snelheid\">Laadsnelheid and laadvermogen\u003c/a>\u003c/li> \u003cli>\u003ca href=\"#begrip-eenheden\">kW, kWh and kWp\u003c/a>\u003c/li> \u003cli>\u003ca href=\"#begrip-klassen\">N1, N2, N3 and Euro 6 / Euro VI\u003c/a>\u003c/li> \u003cli>\u003ca href=\"#begrip-kosten\">Total cost, residual value and Cheaper from\u003c/a>\u003c/li> \u003cli>\u003ca href=\"#begrip-regelingen\">AanZET, MIA, SPRILA and ERE&#39;s\u003c/a>\u003c/li> \u003c/ul> \u003ch2>Charging and electricity\u003c/h2> \u003cp id=\"begrip-acdc\">\u003cb>AC and DC:\u003c/b> AC means charging with alternating current from a standard charge point, usually more slowly. DC means fast charging with direct current from a fast charger.\u003c/p> \u003cp id=\"begrip-mcs\">\u003cb>CCS and MCS:\u003c/b> CCS is the standard fast-charging connector for European trucks and vans. MCS (Megawatt Charging System) is the new connector for heavy trucks, designed to add a lot of charge very quickly during a break.\u003c/p> \u003cp id=\"begrip-snelheid\">\u003cb>Charging speed and payload:\u003c/b> charging speed is how fast a vehicle or charge point can charge, in kilowatts (kW). Payload is something else: how many kilograms you may carry in the vehicle, as shown on the registration document.\u003c/p> \u003cp id=\"begrip-eenheden\">\u003cb>kW, kWh and kWp:\u003c/b> kW is how fast electricity flows (power), kWh is how much electricity (the amount in a battery or used per trip) and kWp is the peak output of solar panels.\u003c/p> \u003cp>\u003cb>Grid congestion:\u003c/b> the electricity grid in an area is full, so you cannot get a larger connection, or only after a wait.\u003c/p> \u003ch2>Vehicle and range\u003c/h2> \u003cp id=\"begrip-wltp\">\u003cb>WLTP:\u003c/b> the official test method manufacturers use to quote range and consumption. In practice you usually get less, especially in winter and with heavy loads.\u003c/p> \u003cp>\u003cb>Usable battery capacity:\u003c/b> the part of the battery you can actually use. Gross is the whole battery; usable (net) is what remains after the margin the manufacturer holds back.\u003c/p> \u003cp id=\"begrip-klassen\">\u003cb>N1, N2 and N3:\u003c/b> European weight classes. N1 is up to 3,500 kg (vans), N2 up to 12 tonnes and N3 above that (trucks). \u003cb>Euro 6 and Euro VI\u003c/b> are diesel emission standards: Euro 6 for vans, Euro VI for trucks. The higher the standard, the cleaner the vehicle and the longer it may enter zero-emission zones.\u003c/p> \u003ch2>Costs and rules\u003c/h2> \u003cp id=\"begrip-kosten\">\u003cb>Total costs:\u003c/b> All costs of One Vehicle over de tijd dat je het hebt: Purchase min Grant and residual value, plus Energy, Maintenance, Insurance, Road tax and heffing. In de sector heet dit vaak TCO. \u003cb>Residual value\u003c/b> is what the vehicle is still worth when you sell it at the end. \u003cb>Electric is cheaper from\u003c/b> is the tipping point: for example from how many kilometres a year, or from which diesel price, electric becomes cheaper.\u003c/p> \u003cp id=\"begrip-regelingen\">\u003cb>AanZET, MIA, SPRILA and EREs:\u003c/b> AanZET is a grant towards a new electric truck, MIA is an extra deduction from your profit, SPRILA is a grant for charge points at your own premises, and EREs are units you can sell for electricity charged into your own vehicles.\u003c/p> \u003cp>\u003cb>Kilometre charge (truck toll):\u003c/b> a charge per kilometre driven for trucks over 3,500 kg. Electric trucks pay a lower rate. \u003cb>ETS2\u003c/b> is a European CO2 charge that will be included in the diesel price from 2027. \u003cb>Zero-emission zone:\u003c/b> an area in a city centre that only vehicles without emissions may enter.\u003c/p> \u003cp>\u003cb>Finance lease and operational lease:\u003c/b> with a finance lease you eventually own the vehicle yourself. With an operational lease the leasing company remains the owner and you pay a fixed monthly amount.\u003c/p> \u003ca class=\"gcl\" href=\"/en/detailed-calculation/\">Run the numbers with your own figures\u003c/a> \u003c/article>\n\n    \u003cnav class=\"gnx\" id=\"gNx\" aria-label=\"Volgend onderwerp\">\u003c/nav>\n   \u003c/div>\n   \u003caside class=\"grl\">\n    \u003cnav aria-label=\"Onderwerpen\" id=\"gRl\">\u003c/nav>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"ad\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\">Advertisement\u003c/div>\n   \u003c/aside>\n  \u003c/div>\n \u003c/div>\n\u003c/section>","nieuws":"\u003csection class=\"page\" data-page=\"nieuws\" hidden>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap\">\n  \u003cdiv class=\"phead\">\u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Electric commercial vehicle news\u003c/h1>\u003cp class=\"seo-intro\">What do changes to truck tolls, energy prices and regulations mean for your business? Check the publication date of each article and calculate the impact using your own figures.\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"tl\">\n   \u003carticle class=\"tli soon\">\u003ctime datetime=\"2028-01-01\">1 January 2028\u003c/time>\u003cspan class=\"kick2\">CO₂ price\u003c/span>\u003ch2>ETS2 for transport fuels\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Fuel suppliers will pay for diesel CO₂ emissions. At €50 per tonne, that adds roughly 13 cents per litre.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"src\">\u003ca href=\"https://www.evupdate.nl/elektrisch-rijden/artikel/automobilisten-kunnen-opgelucht-ademhalen-extra-co-heffing-op-brandstof-komt-pas-in-2028\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Source: EV Update\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/article>\n   \u003carticle class=\"tli lng\">\u003ctime datetime=\"2026-10-16\">16 October 2026\u003c/time>\u003cspan class=\"kick2\">Costs\u003c/span>\u003ch2>\u003cbutton class=\"tlb\" type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\">ABN AMRO: 2026 is the tipping point\u003c/button>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"tlx\">\u003cp>According to ABN AMRO, electric road transport breaks through in 2026. Tax incentives, better technology and high fuel prices make electric trucks more attractive. A heavy Euro 6 diesel truck pays about €0.21 truck toll per kilometre, an electric one €0.04. For trips within the Netherlands, which mostly stay within 500 km, electric can therefore be cheaper. It does still cost about three times as much to buy.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The Netherlands is ahead. In the first half of 2026, 16.3% of new trucks were electric, against 4.8% across the EU. For new vans it was 83.7%.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The bottleneck is now the plug, not the truck. Grid congestion means many hauliers cannot get a heavier connection. ABN AMRO points to smart control of solar power, battery storage and chargers, and to contracts that let you use extra capacity between midnight and 6 am.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Haulier Weduwe J. de Bruijn en Zonen, with 55 trucks, already runs four electric trucks. According to the company they are already cheaper than diesel, for trucks that charge at home overnight and drive more than 300 km a day. It aims to have 25 to 30 electric trucks around 2030.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"src\">\u003ca href=\"https://www.abnamro.nl/nl/zakelijk/insights/sectoren-en-trends/logistiek/kantelpunt-2026-elektrificatie-breekt-door-in-wegtransport.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Source: ABN AMRO\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003c/article>\n   \u003carticle class=\"tli\">\u003ctime datetime=\"2026-10-09\">9 October 2026\u003c/time>\u003cspan class=\"kick2\">Fuel duty\u003c/span>\u003ch2>Diesel duty reduction proposed for 2027\u003c/h2>\u003cp>The Dutch government proposes extending the diesel duty reduction in 2027, at €0.552 per litre. Proposed duty is €0.616 in 2028 and €0.701 from 2029. Parliament votes on 12 November.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"src\">\u003ca href=\"https://www.taxence.nl/nieuws/tweede-nota-van-wijziging-belastingplan-2027/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Source: Taxence\u003c/a>\u003ca href=\"/en/\">Check the numbers\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/article>\n   \u003carticle class=\"tli lng\">\u003ctime datetime=\"2026-09-16\">16 September 2026\u003c/time>\u003cspan class=\"kick2\">Charging\u003c/span>\u003ch2>\u003cbutton class=\"tlb\" type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\">Share your charging depot with other hauliers\u003c/button>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"tlx\">\u003cp>In the first half of 2026, almost 172,000 new trucks were registered in the EU, 9.8% more than a year earlier. Electric truck registrations rose 47.7%, to 4.8% of the market. Germany, the Netherlands and France together account for 74% of electric trucks. In the Netherlands the number grew 44.5%.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Vornfeld sees charging as the biggest bottleneck now. Grants help, but can also slow things down. In Germany, three funding calls for charging infrastructure worth around €300 million in total were heavily oversubscribed, and many hauliers are now waiting. The advice: build a depot that pays off without a grant.\u003c/p>\u003cp>That works best when the depot is used a lot. A charger that sits idle overnight is money that earns nothing. That is why some hauliers open their depot to other hauliers.\u003c/p>\u003cp>One example is Alfredsson Transport in Norrköping, Sweden. The depot charges its own fleet and is open to other hauliers, including megawatt charging (MCS). Instead of waiting for a heavier grid connection, the company installed a 1.2 MW battery and 400 kWp of solar panels.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"src\">\u003ca href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/utilization-imperative-how-shared-depots-flexible-drive-vornfeld-314ze/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Source: Vornfeld on LinkedIn\u003c/a>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/charging/\">Switching guide\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003c/article>\n   \u003carticle class=\"tli lng\">\u003ctime datetime=\"2026-09-08\">8 September 2026\u003c/time>\u003cspan class=\"kick2\">Research\u003c/span>\u003ch2>\u003cbutton class=\"tlb\" type=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\">Electric long haul up to 15% cheaper\u003c/button>\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"tlx\">\u003cp>Bain &amp; Company surveyed 507 fleet decision makers in Germany, France, the United Kingdom, Italy and Poland. More than 60% expect their fleet to grow over the next three years.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For long haul, Bain finds electric has largely reached cost parity with diesel or is cheaper. In Germany, a heavy electric tractor unit costs up to 15% less over five years, mainly thanks to lower energy costs and toll savings. What still holds operators back: too few public chargers, high purchase prices, less flexibility and long charging times.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Operators expect diesel to make up about half of new truck sales in 2030 and a third in 2035. Hydrogen stays a niche until 2035. When choosing an electric truck, charging speed weighs more than reliability.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Notably, one in three operators has been in contact with a Chinese manufacturer and is likely to buy one within three years. 61% expect Chinese trucks to be 10 to 30% cheaper. Brand trust, service and residual value are still their weak points.\u003c/p>\u003cdiv class=\"src\">\u003ca href=\"https://www.bain.com/insights/european-truck-market-outlook-2026/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Source: Bain &amp; Company\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003c/article>\n  \u003c/div>\n  \u003caside class=\"ad band\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\">Advertisement\u003c/aside>\n \u003c/div>\n\u003c/section>","over":"\u003csection class=\"page\" data-page=\"over\" hidden>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap\">\n  \u003cdiv class=\"phead\">\u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">You want to know what it costs, not what it promises\u003c/h1>\u003c/div>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"oostory\">\n   \u003cp class=\"oolead\">Every dealer tells you their electric truck pays for itself. Every diesel seller says it&#39;s still too early. Who is right? That depends on your routes, your kilometres and your business.\u003c/p>\n   \u003cp>We ran into the same thing when we went looking for the answer. There was no independent comparison that took everything into account. So we got to work ourselves and built a calculation model that includes everything.\u003c/p>\n   \u003cp>You enter how you drive, and you see what diesel and electric cost you, including purchase and financing, energy, maintenance, toll and grants.\u003c/p>\n   \u003cp>And we keep it current. When the truck toll changes, a new grant round opens or a new model comes to market, we update the figures.\u003c/p>\n   \u003cdiv class=\"ooqd\">\n    \u003ch3>We work out those questions for you too\u003c/h3>\n    \u003cul>\n     \u003cli>\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003ccircle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"4\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M12 2v2M12 20v2M2 12h2M20 12h2M4.9 4.9l1.4 1.4M17.7 17.7l1.4 1.4M4.9 19.1l1.4-1.4M17.7 6.3l1.4-1.4\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003cspan>What if you generate your own power?\u003c/span>\u003c/li>\n     \u003cli>\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 21V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16M3 21h12M6 9h6M14 8l3 3v6a2 2 0 0 0 4 0V9l-3-3\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003cspan>What if diesel gets more expensive because of the CO₂ price from 2028?\u003c/span>\u003c/li>\n     \u003cli>\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003crect x=\"3\" y=\"5\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003cspan>When should you replace each vehicle?\u003c/span>\u003c/li>\n    \u003c/ul>\n   \u003c/div>\n   \u003cp>So you make the choice based on numbers.\u003c/p>\n  \u003c/div>\n  \u003ch2 class=\"ooth\">Who we are\u003c/h2>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"oot oots\">\n   \u003carticle class=\"oof\">\n    \u003cdiv class=\"ooh\">\u003cspan class=\"oom\" aria-hidden=\"true\">JV\u003c/span>\u003cdiv>\u003ch3 data-no-translate>Jan Veraart\u003c/h3>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cp>Jan does the maths. He graduated in mathematical optimisation in logistics and won the Jo van Nunen Thesis Award for it.\u003c/p>\n    \u003cp class=\"oox\" data-no-translate>Erasmus Universiteit · TU Eindhoven · BMW Group · Rijkswaterstaat\u003c/p>\n   \u003c/article>\n   \u003carticle class=\"oof\">\n    \u003cdiv class=\"ooh\">\u003cspan class=\"oom\" aria-hidden=\"true\">MD\u003c/span>\u003cdiv>\u003ch3 data-no-translate>Max van Dam\u003c/h3>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cp>Max knows the rules. He holds a master&#39;s degree in administrative and tax law and knows which grants exist and how the rules fit together.\u003c/p>\n    \u003cp class=\"oox\" data-no-translate>Universiteit Leiden\u003c/p>\n   \u003c/article>\n  \u003c/div>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"ooc\">\u003ca class=\"cta\" href=\"/en/fleet-analysis/\">\u003cspan>Discuss your fleet\u003c/span>\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/a>\u003ca href=\"mailto:info@stekkerofdiesel.nl\" data-no-translate>info@stekkerofdiesel.nl\u003c/a>\u003c/div>\n  \u003caside class=\"ad band\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\">Advertisement\u003c/aside>\n \u003c/div>\n\u003c/section>","vloot":"\u003csection class=\"page\" data-page=\"vloot\" hidden>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap vz\">\n  \u003cdiv class=\"vzh\">\u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Fleet analysis: electrify your fleet, costs and planning\u003c/h1>\u003cp>With a fleet analysis we assess which vehicles can go electric, using your own routes and figures. You get a plan with costs, charging requirements and concrete next steps.\u003c/p>\u003csvg class=\"vzm\" viewBox=\"0 0 1128 250\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A route from the depot through a zero-emission zone past a fast charger to the customer\">\n\u003cpath d=\"M70 200 C220 200,250 110,400 110 S600 190,740 160 S930 70,1060 90\" class=\"road\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M70 200 C220 200,250 110,400 110 S600 190,740 160 S930 70,1060 90\" class=\"mid\"/>\n\u003cg class=\"dep\">\u003cpath d=\"M30 214V170l40-22 40 22v44z\"/>\u003crect x=\"58\" y=\"188\" width=\"24\" height=\"26\"/>\u003c/g>\u003crect x=\"114\" y=\"176\" width=\"10\" height=\"30\" rx=\"2\" class=\"ch\"/>\n\u003ccircle cx=\"540\" cy=\"150\" r=\"74\" class=\"zone\"/>\u003cg class=\"city\">\u003crect x=\"500\" y=\"96\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" rx=\"2\"/>\u003crect x=\"528\" y=\"86\" width=\"18\" height=\"44\" rx=\"2\"/>\u003crect x=\"556\" y=\"104\" width=\"24\" height=\"26\" rx=\"2\"/>\u003crect x=\"586\" y=\"120\" width=\"16\" height=\"22\" rx=\"2\"/>\u003crect x=\"504\" y=\"180\" width=\"26\" height=\"22\" rx=\"2\"/>\u003crect x=\"540\" y=\"190\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/>\u003c/g>\n\u003cg transform=\"translate(760 108)\">\u003crect width=\"18\" height=\"36\" rx=\"3\" class=\"ch\"/>\u003cg class=\"blt\" transform=\"translate(9 14) scale(.9)\">\u003cpath d=\"M1.6 -7.5L-4.2 1.6H-0.2L-1.6 7.5L4.2 -1.6H0.2Z\"/>\u003c/g>\u003c/g>\n\u003cg class=\"dep\">\u003cpath d=\"M1040 106V66h70v40z\"/>\u003crect x=\"1052\" y=\"80\" width=\"22\" height=\"26\"/>\u003c/g>\n\u003cg transform=\"translate(250 104)\" class=\"trk\">\u003csvg width=\"96\" height=\"40\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--card)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/g>\n\u003cg class=\"b6n\" data-s=\"1\" transform=\"translate(70 130)\">\u003ccircle r=\"24\" class=\"hl\"/>\u003ccircle r=\"14\"/>\u003ctext y=\"5\">1\u003c/text>\u003c/g>\u003cg class=\"b6n\" data-s=\"2\" transform=\"translate(300 82)\">\u003ccircle r=\"24\" class=\"hl\"/>\u003ccircle r=\"14\"/>\u003ctext y=\"5\">2\u003c/text>\u003c/g>\u003cg class=\"b6n\" data-s=\"3\" transform=\"translate(540 58)\">\u003ccircle r=\"24\" class=\"hl\"/>\u003ccircle r=\"14\"/>\u003ctext y=\"5\">3\u003c/text>\u003c/g>\u003cg class=\"b6n\" data-s=\"4\" transform=\"translate(769 84)\">\u003ccircle r=\"24\" class=\"hl\"/>\u003ccircle r=\"14\"/>\u003ctext y=\"5\">4\u003c/text>\u003c/g>\u003cg class=\"b6n\" data-s=\"5\" transform=\"translate(1075 44)\">\u003ccircle r=\"24\" class=\"hl\"/>\u003ccircle r=\"14\"/>\u003ctext y=\"5\">5\u003c/text>\u003c/g>\n\u003c/svg>\u003c/div>\n  \u003caside class=\"vzf\">\n   \u003cform class=\"ffm\" id=\"fForm\" novalidate>\n    \u003cdiv class=\"vzfh\">\u003ch2>Book an intro call\u003c/h2>\u003cp class=\"vzfp\">Free introductory call, fleet advice from \u003cb>€ 795\u003c/b> excl. VAT\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\n    \u003clabel class=\"ff\">\u003cspan>Name\u003c/span>\u003cinput name=\"contact_name\" required maxlength=\"200\" autocomplete=\"name\">\u003c/label>\n    \u003clabel class=\"ff\">\u003cspan>Company\u003c/span>\u003cinput name=\"company\" required maxlength=\"200\" autocomplete=\"organization\">\u003c/label>\n    \u003clabel class=\"ff\">\u003cspan>Email\u003c/span>\u003cinput name=\"email\" type=\"email\" required maxlength=\"200\" autocomplete=\"email\">\u003c/label>\n    \u003clabel class=\"ff\">\u003cspan>Phone\u003c/span>\u003cinput name=\"phone\" type=\"tel\" maxlength=\"50\" autocomplete=\"tel\">\u003c/label>\n    \u003clabel class=\"ff\">\u003cspan>Message\u003c/span>\u003ctextarea name=\"message\" id=\"fMsg\" rows=\"2\" maxlength=\"4000\">\u003c/textarea>\u003c/label>\n    \u003cfieldset class=\"ffs\">\u003clegend>Number of vehicles\u003c/legend>\u003cdiv class=\"seg\">\u003clabel>\u003cinput type=\"radio\" name=\"fleet_size\" value=\"1-5\">\u003cspan>1–5\u003c/span>\u003c/label>\u003clabel>\u003cinput type=\"radio\" name=\"fleet_size\" value=\"6-20\" checked>\u003cspan>6–20\u003c/span>\u003c/label>\u003clabel>\u003cinput type=\"radio\" name=\"fleet_size\" value=\"21-50\">\u003cspan>21–50\u003c/span>\u003c/label>\u003clabel>\u003cinput type=\"radio\" name=\"fleet_size\" value=\"50+\">\u003cspan>50+\u003c/span>\u003c/label>\u003c/div>\u003c/fieldset>\n    \u003cinput class=\"fhp\" name=\"website\" tabindex=\"-1\" autocomplete=\"off\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n    \u003cp class=\"ferr\" id=\"fErr\" role=\"alert\" hidden>\u003c/p>\n    \u003cbutton class=\"cta\" type=\"submit\" id=\"fSend\">\u003cspan>Get in touch\u003c/span>\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/button>\n    \u003cp class=\"fnote\">No obligation · \u003ca href=\"/en/privacy/\">Privacy\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\n   \u003c/form>\n   \u003cdiv class=\"ffm fok\" id=\"fOk\" hidden tabindex=\"-1\">\u003ch2>Thank you\u003c/h2>\u003cp>We will contact you within 1 working day.\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\n  \u003c/aside>\n  \u003csection class=\"vzs\">\u003ch2>How it works\u003c/h2>\u003col>\u003cli class=\"vzs1\">\u003cb>Fill in the form\u003c/b>\u003cspan>Name, company and the size of your fleet.\u003c/span>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003cb>We get in touch\u003c/b>\u003cspan>Within 1 working day, by phone or email.\u003c/span>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003cb>Introduction\u003c/b>\u003cspan>About your vehicles, routes and planning.\u003c/span>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003cb>Your fleet plan\u003c/b>\u003cspan>Calculated per vehicle and discussed together.\u003c/span>\u003c/li>\u003c/ol>\u003c/section>\n  \u003csection class=\"vzv\">\u003ch2>What it gets you\u003c/h2>\u003cul>\u003cli>\u003csvg class=\"ic\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M12 3l8 3v6c0 5-3.5 8-8 9-4.5-1-8-4-8-9V6z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M8.5 12l2.5 2.5 4.5-5\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003cdiv>\u003ch3>Insight into your investment\u003c/h3>\u003cp>Per vehicle, the \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/buy-lease-or-rent/\">total cost over the full term\u003c/a>, diesel alongside electric. With sources, assumptions and ranges to support your decision.\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003csvg class=\"ic\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M6 3h9l4 4v14H6z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M15 3v4h4M9 13l2 2 4-4\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003cdiv>\u003ch3>Grants and conditions explained\u003c/h3>\u003cp>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/grants/\">AanZET and MIA\u003c/a> cannot be combined for the same investment. We check the conditions that apply and also calculate without grants or ERE income.\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003csvg class=\"ic\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003crect x=\"3\" y=\"5\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M7 14h3M7 17h3M13 14h4\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003cdiv>\u003ch3>An informed replacement plan\u003c/h3>\u003cp>A replacement plan that fits depreciation, lease contracts, delivery times and the \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/zero-emission-zones/\">zero-emission zones\u003c/a> you drive in.\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003csvg class=\"ic\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003crect x=\"5\" y=\"3\" width=\"10\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M11 7l-3 5h4l-3 5\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M15 9h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v5a2 2 0 0 0 4 0\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003cdiv>\u003ch3>A charging plan for your site\u003c/h3>\u003cp>We assess chargers and power against your routes, meter data and grid contract. We also consider \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/grid-capacity/\">grid congestion\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\u003c/section>\n  \u003csection class=\"vzp\">\u003ch2>What you get\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"vzpg\">\u003csvg class=\"vxd vzpd\" viewBox=\"0 0 260 320\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003crect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"240\" height=\"300\" rx=\"8\" class=\"pg\"/>\u003crect x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"240\" height=\"6\" rx=\"3\" class=\"gb\"/>\u003cg data-p=\"1\">\u003crect x=\"26\" y=\"32\" width=\"120\" height=\"10\" rx=\"3\" class=\"tl\"/>\u003crect x=\"26\" y=\"48\" width=\"180\" height=\"5\" rx=\"2.5\" class=\"ln\"/>\u003crect x=\"26\" y=\"58\" width=\"140\" height=\"5\" rx=\"2.5\" class=\"ln\"/>\u003c/g>\u003cg data-p=\"2\">\u003cg class=\"ta\">\u003csvg x=\"26\" y=\"72\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/g>\u003cg class=\"ta\">\u003csvg x=\"68\" y=\"72\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/g>\u003cg class=\"tg\">\u003csvg x=\"110\" y=\"72\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/g>\u003cg class=\"tg\">\u003csvg x=\"152\" y=\"72\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/g>\u003cg class=\"tg\">\u003csvg x=\"194\" y=\"72\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/g>\u003cg class=\"tg\">\u003csvg x=\"26\" y=\"94\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/g>\u003cg class=\"ta\">\u003csvg x=\"68\" y=\"94\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/g>\u003cg class=\"tg\">\u003csvg x=\"110\" y=\"94\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/g>\u003cg class=\"tg\">\u003csvg x=\"152\" y=\"94\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/g>\u003cg class=\"tg\">\u003csvg x=\"194\" y=\"94\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 64 28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 4h36v17H4z\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M40 9h10l6 7v5H40\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"13\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"22\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--page)\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/g>\u003c/g>\u003cline x1=\"26\" y1=\"124\" x2=\"234\" y2=\"124\" class=\"hr\"/>\u003cg data-p=\"3\">\u003crect x=\"26\" y=\"138\" width=\"150\" height=\"12\" rx=\"3\" class=\"bd\"/>\u003crect x=\"26\" y=\"156\" width=\"104\" height=\"12\" rx=\"3\" class=\"be\"/>\u003c/g>\u003cg data-p=\"4\">\u003ccircle cx=\"212\" cy=\"153\" r=\"20\" class=\"st\"/>\u003cpath d=\"M203 153l6 6 11-11\" class=\"ck\"/>\u003c/g>\u003cline x1=\"26\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"234\" y2=\"184\" class=\"hr\"/>\u003cg data-p=\"5\">\u003cpath d=\"M26 222H234\" class=\"hr\"/>\u003crect x=\"30\" y=\"194\" width=\"16\" height=\"28\" rx=\"3\" class=\"be\"/>\u003cg class=\"bw\" transform=\"translate(38 206) scale(.8)\">\u003cpath d=\"M1.6 -7.5L-4.2 1.6H-0.2L-1.6 7.5L4.2 -1.6H0.2Z\"/>\u003c/g>\u003crect x=\"60\" y=\"194\" width=\"16\" height=\"28\" rx=\"3\" class=\"be\"/>\u003cg class=\"bw\" transform=\"translate(68 206) scale(.8)\">\u003cpath d=\"M1.6 -7.5L-4.2 1.6H-0.2L-1.6 7.5L4.2 -1.6H0.2Z\"/>\u003c/g>\u003crect x=\"90\" y=\"194\" width=\"16\" height=\"28\" rx=\"3\" class=\"be\"/>\u003cg class=\"bw\" transform=\"translate(98 206) scale(.8)\">\u003cpath d=\"M1.6 -7.5L-4.2 1.6H-0.2L-1.6 7.5L4.2 -1.6H0.2Z\"/>\u003c/g>\u003crect x=\"120\" y=\"194\" width=\"16\" height=\"28\" rx=\"3\" class=\"be\"/>\u003cg class=\"bw\" transform=\"translate(128 206) scale(.8)\">\u003cpath d=\"M1.6 -7.5L-4.2 1.6H-0.2L-1.6 7.5L4.2 -1.6H0.2Z\"/>\u003c/g>\u003cpath d=\"M150 222V200l30-12 30 12v22\" class=\"ol\"/>\u003c/g>\u003cline x1=\"26\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"234\" y2=\"236\" class=\"hr\"/>\u003cg data-p=\"6\">\u003cline x1=\"30\" y1=\"282\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"282\" class=\"tlx\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"48\" cy=\"282\" r=\"5\" class=\"bd\"/>\u003crect x=\"34\" y=\"252\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" rx=\"3\" class=\"bd\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"100\" cy=\"282\" r=\"5\" class=\"bd\"/>\u003crect x=\"86\" y=\"252\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" rx=\"3\" class=\"bd\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"160\" cy=\"282\" r=\"5\" class=\"be\"/>\u003crect x=\"146\" y=\"252\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" rx=\"3\" class=\"be\"/>\u003ccircle cx=\"212\" cy=\"282\" r=\"5\" class=\"be\"/>\u003crect x=\"198\" y=\"252\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" rx=\"3\" class=\"be\"/>\u003c/g>\u003c/svg>\u003cdiv>\u003ch3>Your fleet plan\u003c/h3>\u003cp>A report per vehicle and per location, which we go through with you.\u003c/p>\u003col>\u003cli data-p=\"1\">\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/checklist/\">\u003cspan>Summary and advice\u003c/span>\u003cem>Step-by-step plan\u003c/em>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli data-p=\"2\">\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/range-planning/\">\u003cspan>Feasibility by vehicle and route\u003c/span>\u003cem>Range\u003c/em>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli data-p=\"3\">\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/buy-lease-or-rent/\">\u003cspan>Costs over the full term\u003c/span>\u003cem>Buy or lease\u003c/em>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli data-p=\"4\">\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/grants/\">\u003cspan>Grants and when to apply\u003c/span>\u003cem>Grants\u003c/em>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli data-p=\"5\">\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/charging/\">\u003cspan>Charging plan for each site\u003c/span>\u003cem>Charging\u003c/em>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli data-p=\"6\">\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/zero-emission-zones/\">\u003cspan>Annual replacement plan\u003c/span>\u003cem>Zero-emission zones\u003c/em>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003c/ol>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv class=\"vzseo\">\u003ch2>What is a fleet analysis?\u003c/h2>\u003cp>A fleet analysis maps out your entire fleet and works out, per vehicle, what diesel and electric cost over the service life. Not with averages, but with your own annual mileage, daily routes, loads and energy prices. That shows which commercial vehicles can already go electric, which are better replaced later and what that means for your cost per kilometre.\u003c/p>\u003ch3>What do we calculate?\u003c/h3>\u003cp>Per vehicle we compare the total costs: purchase or lease, energy, maintenance, road tax and residual value. We test the range against your longest daily route, include battery degradation over the years and calculate how many charging points and how much power your site needs. Grants and access to \u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/zero-emission-zones/\">zero-emission zones\u003c/a> also factor into the replacement order.\u003c/p>\u003ch3>Who is it for?\u003c/h3>\u003cp>For companies with several vans, rigid trucks or tractor units that want to know where they stand before requesting quotes. Want to work through one vehicle yourself first? Start with the \u003ca href=\"/en/\">Calculator\u003c/a>. For the whole fleet, request a fleet analysis below.\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"vzseo\">\u003ch2>Diesel or electric: assess each vehicle\u003c/h2>\u003cp>Lower energy costs only help when operations still work. We compare lifetime costs, cost per km and required investment, alongside daily routes, payload, customer access and charging windows.\u003c/p>\u003ch3>A replacement plan with clear assumptions\u003c/h3>\u003cp>See which vehicles can switch now and which should follow later. We show what changes with different energy prices, lower residual values or no grant. The results provide a basis for quotes and investment decisions.\u003c/p>\u003cp>\u003ca href=\"/en/\">Start with your own cost calculation\u003c/a> · \u003ca href=\"#fForm\">Discuss your fleet with us\u003c/a>\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\u003c/section>\n\n  \u003csection class=\"vzr\">\u003ch2>What we check on each route\u003c/h2>\u003col>\u003cli data-s=\"1\">\u003cb>Depot\u003c/b>\u003cspan>Charging overnight while the vehicles are parked. With your grid connection and number of chargers.\u003c/span>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/grid-capacity/\">Grid congestion\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli data-s=\"2\">\u003cb>En route\u003c/b>\u003cspan>Range with your load, and the higher consumption in winter.\u003c/span>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/range-planning/\">Range\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli data-s=\"3\">\u003cb>Zero-emission zone\u003c/b>\u003cspan>Which zones are on your routes and until when your diesel may still enter.\u003c/span>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/zero-emission-zones/\">Zero-emission zones\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli data-s=\"4\">\u003cb>Fast charger\u003c/b>\u003cspan>Charging en route with CCS or MCS, when a trip is longer than the battery allows.\u003c/span>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/charging/\">Charging\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli data-s=\"5\">\u003cb>Customer\u003c/b>\u003cspan>A customer stop can provide a charging opportunity when time, access and charging power are confirmed.\u003c/span>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/charging/\">Charging\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003c/ol>\u003c/section>\n  \u003csection class=\"vzt\">\u003ch2>What will a fleet transition plan give you?\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"vzt2\" id=\"vzT\">\u003c/div>\u003c/section>\n    \u003csection class=\"vzk\">\u003ch2>Why Stekker of Diesel\u003c/h2>\u003cp class=\"vzkl\">Independent fleet advice. We sell no vehicles and have no brand preference.\u003c/p>\u003cul>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/models/\">\u003cb data-mcount>67\u003c/b>\u003cspan>Electric vehicles in onze catalogus\u003c/span>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/switching-guide/\">\u003cb>12\u003c/b>\u003cspan>topics researched in the Switching guide\u003c/span>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/about/\">\u003cb>Sources\u003c/b>\u003cspan>and assumptions made clear\u003c/span>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003cli>\u003ca href=\"/en/\">\u003cb>Open\u003c/b>\u003cspan>cost inputs from the calculator\u003c/span>\u003c/a>\u003c/li>\u003c/ul>\u003c/section>\n  \u003csection class=\"vzq\">\u003ch2>Frequently asked questions about fleet analysis and fleet advice\u003c/h2>\u003cdiv class=\"vzqg\">\u003cdetails open>\u003csummary>\u003ch3>Is a fleet analysis the same as fleet advice?\u003c/h3>\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Almost. The fleet analysis is the calculation itself: per vehicle we set out costs, range, charging and replacement timing. The fleet advice is the plan that follows from it, with a replacement order and concrete steps. We deliver both in one engagement. A fleet analysis is also called a vehicle fleet analysis.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\u003cdetails>\u003csummary>\u003ch3>What data do you need for a fleet analysis?\u003c/h3>\u003c/summary>\u003cp>Your current vehicles, your annual mileage and daily routes, your energy and diesel prices and your charging locations. If you do not have everything to hand, we work with assumptions that we test together in the introductory meeting.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\u003cdetails>\u003csummary>\u003ch3>What does a fleet analysis cost?\u003c/h3>\u003c/summary>\u003cp>That depends on the number of vehicles and locations we work through. The introductory meeting is without obligation; after that you hear in advance what the analysis costs, before we start.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\u003cdetails>\u003csummary>\u003ch3>Which vehicles is a fleet analysis suitable for?\u003c/h3>\u003c/summary>\u003cp>For vans, rigid trucks, tractor units and buses, from a few vehicles to a complete fleet. Even if part of your fleet keeps running on diesel for now, the analysis shows where electric already pays off and where it does not yet.\u003c/p>\u003c/details>\u003c/div>\u003c/section>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"vzc\">\u003cbutton class=\"cta\" type=\"button\" id=\"fGo\">\u003cspan>Book an intro call\u003c/span>\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003cpath d=\"M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6\"/>\u003c/svg>\u003c/button>\u003cspan>Reply within 1 working day\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\n \u003c/div>\n\u003c/section>","privacy":"\u003csection class=\"page\" data-page=\"privacy\" hidden>\n \u003cdiv class=\"wrap\">\n  \u003cdiv class=\"phead\">\u003ch1 tabindex=\"-1\">Privacy policy\u003c/h1>\u003c/div>\n  \u003cdiv class=\"prose\">\n   \u003cp>Stekker of Diesel (stekkerofdiesel.nl) is a free calculator. This policy explains which data is processed and why. Last updated 2 November 2026.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>What we don&#39;t ask for\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>You do not need an account to use the calculator. We do not ask for your name, email address or other personal information.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>Request a fleet analysis\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>For a fleet analysis enquiry, we store your name, company, email, phone number and message. We use these only to contact you and do not share them with others. Data is held in a restricted environment at Supabase and deleted within 12 months of our last contact, or earlier on request.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>Business email from us\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>If we email your company about Stekker of Diesel, we found your business email address on your company website or in a public business register. We store the address with the company name, your name if it is listed with the address, the type of transport and where we found the address. We do this on the basis of our legitimate interest: pointing transport companies to a free, independent cost comparison. If you click a link in the email, we record which link and when, so we can see which emails are useful. If you consent to statistics on the site, we link your visit to that click so we can see which pages you view. Without that consent we do not. We do not track whether you open an email.\u003c/p>\n   \u003cp>You can unsubscribe with the link at the bottom of every email or via info@stekkerofdiesel.nl. After that we will not email you again and only keep your email address on a suppression list, so it stays that way. We delete the other data no later than twelve months after our last email. You can also ask which data we hold, have it corrected or have it deleted.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>PDF of je berekening\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>Wil je je berekening als PDF, dan questions we eenmalig je e-mailadres. We bewaren dat met het soort Vehicle, de taal and One link naar je berekening, and gebruiken het alleen om je over je PDF te kunnen mailen. Vink je News on, dan sturen we je af and toe News over Grants and nieuwe Vehicles; afmelden kan in elke mail. De Data staan in One afgeschermde omgeving At Supabase and worden after 25 months verwijderd.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>Request a quote\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>If you request a model quote, we store your name, company, email, phone number, chosen model and calculation link. We share these contact details with dealers of that brand to obtain quotes for you. We delete the data within 12 months of our last contact.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>Price alerts and sale price reports\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>For a price alert, we store your email, vehicle category and maximum price so we can email matching offers. Each email contains an unsubscribe link; unsubscribing deletes your details. Reported sale prices are stored without names, email addresses or registration numbers, solely for the residual-value index.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>Registration number\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>Your browser retrieves public vehicle data directly from RDW. The registration number stays only in your browser so you can continue later. Saved calculations contain vehicle category, make, model, year, weight and Euro class, never the registration number.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>Your calculations\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>We store calculations to improve the calculator: inputs and changes, vehicle selection, results, device type, screen width and referral source. Without analytics consent, these are anonymous, with no visitor identifier or device storage. With consent, your visitor identifier is included. Calculations are held in our Supabase database for up to 25 months.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>Your cookie choices\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>On your first visit, we ask permission to use cookies and similar technologies for analytics and personalised ads. You can control these separately. Your choice is stored in your browser for 12 months. Use Cookies in the footer to change or withdraw consent.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>Analytics, only with your consent\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>With consent, we measure pages viewed, buttons clicked, steps completed, models viewed and calculation results and settings. We also record where on the page you click, how fast pages load, device type, screen size, browser language and time zone, the country you visit from, referral source and campaign codes to improve the calculator.\u003c/p>\n   \u003cp>To distinguish visits, we store a random visitor identifier locally in your browser. It does not identify you and is not linked to other information. We do not store IP addresses. Analytics data is held in our Supabase database for up to 25 months. It also supports A/B tests, where visitors may see different button wording.\u003c/p>\n   \u003cp>With your analytics consent, we also use Google Analytics 4. Google measures page views, approximate location, device and browser, traffic sources and predefined actions, such as viewing models and completing the calculator. Google Analytics does not store raw IP addresses. We do not send Google names, email addresses, number plates, form contents or calculation settings from shared links. Google sets cookies starting with _ga; these expire within twelve months. Event-level and user-level data in Analytics is retained for fourteen months. Withdraw your consent using Cookies to stop Analytics and remove its cookies from your browser.\u003c/p>\n   \u003cp>Without consent, we count page views, how long and how far you scrolled, how fast the page loaded, referral source, country, screen width and whether the device is mobile, and store calculations anonymously. No visitor identifier is assigned or stored on your device. Withdrawing consent removes the visitor identifier from your browser.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>Advertising\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>To keep this site free, we show Google AdSense ads. With consent for personalised ads, Google and its partners may use cookies to tailor ads based on visits to this and other sites. Without that consent, ads are not personalised. We pass your choice through Google Consent Mode. Learn how Google uses data at \u003ca href=\"https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites?hl=nl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">policies.google.com\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>What stays in your browser\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>Your latest calculator settings are stored locally in your browser so you can continue later. This is needed for the calculator to work. Shared links contain calculation settings only, not personal information.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>Third-party services\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>Fonts are served from our own website. Your browser connects to Supabase for current vehicle data. GitHub Pages hosts the website and stores IP addresses in server logs for security. Supabase also receives your IP address when your browser connects. This technical processing is separate from our visitor analytics, where we do not store IP addresses.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>Your rights\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>Under the GDPR, you may access, correct or delete your data and object to processing. Analytics uses a random identifier, so we cannot link it to you personally; withdrawing consent removes that identifier. Ad-related requests are handled through Google. You may complain to the Dutch Data Protection Authority.\u003c/p>\n   \u003ch2>Contact\u003c/h2>\n   \u003cp>Questions about your data or the site? Email \u003ca href=\"mailto:info@stekkerofdiesel.nl\" data-no-translate>info@stekkerofdiesel.nl\u003c/a>.\u003c/p>\n  \u003c/div>\n \u003c/div>\n\u003c/section>"};const app=document.getElementById('app');for(const [key,markup]of Object.entries(pages)){let page=app.querySelector('.page[data-page="'+key+'"]');if(!page){const t=document.createElement('template');t.innerHTML=markup;page=t.content.firstElementChild;page.hidden=true;app.append(page)}else if(key==='gids'){const t=document.createElement('template');t.innerHTML=markup;for(const article of t.content.querySelectorAll('article[data-g]'))if(!page.querySelector('article[data-g="'+article.dataset.g+'"]')){article.hidden=true;page.querySelector('.gm').append(article)}}}})();